333830041,"sha":"fd31ffa416f270f8d65189ffd7e8c2439853ef69"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"codebend3r","providerType":"User"},"email":"cj.rivas.dev@gmail.com","name":"CJ Rivas"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-14T05:33:36Z","committedDate":"2026-08-14T05:33:36Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"codebend3r","providerType":"User"},"email":"cj.rivas.dev@gmail.com","name":"CJ Rivas"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:12:19.112Z","repositoryId":1333830041,"sha":"352fd0fa175cb8e3854a9b85aae9e754ef4ba4b5"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:12:19.112Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1402814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r","id":1402814,"login":"codebend3r","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MDI4MTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commits/18878cadb5ab0ca6112d698989061231e391df83/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T16:39:18Z","email":"cj.rivas.dev@gmail.com","name":"CJ Rivas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T16:39:18Z","email":"cj.rivas.dev@gmail.com","name":"CJ Rivas"},"message":"Give every app its own start and dev script\n\nRunning one app by itself is the honest test of independent deployment,\nbut it was the one thing you had to assemble by hand: a --filter build,\nthen a preview, then a port check that covered all three apps whether you\nwanted them or not. There is now one script per app. start:<app> mirrors\nstart, building that app and serving the build; dev:<app> mirrors dev, on\na Vite dev server with HMR. Shell is an alias for world, so start:shell\nand start:world are the same command.\n\nscripts/start-app.mjs resolves the name, preflights that one port before\nbuilding anything, then hands off to the app''s own dev, build and\npreview. It prints which other apps are answering first, so a remote slot\nthat fails to load reads as a server that is not running rather than a\nbug. Jerry is included even though this repo never builds it: the script\nruns the guest repo''s own scripts, and says what to clone when that repo\nis not checked out next door.\n\nports.mjs is reused rather than duplicated. It now takes app names, so\nthe preflight can cover one port instead of three, exports its probes for\nstart-app.mjs to import, and only dispatches when run directly. Jerry is\nin its table as opt in, named or not touched at all, so bare stop still\nfrees only the three ports this repo owns. That argument reaches stop\nthrough bun run, which makes `bun run stop morty` work as well.","tree":{"sha":"ce212e0bc682062679c4487ccc2dbb15d8d0bdcc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/git/trees/ce212e0bc682062679c4487ccc2dbb15d8d0bdcc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/git/commits/18878cadb5ab0ca6112d698989061231e391df83","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1402814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r","id":1402814,"login":"codebend3r","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MDI4MTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commit/18878cadb5ab0ca6112d698989061231e391df83","node_id":"C_kwDOT4ChmdoAKDE4ODc4Y2FkYjVhYjBjYTYxMTJkNjk4OTg5MDYxMjMxZTM5MWRmODM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commit/1cee3e8f2a561f8e499d6393fb63f9d367a3bbdf","sha":"1cee3e8f2a561f8e499d6393fb63f9d367a3bbdf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commits/1cee3e8f2a561f8e499d6393fb63f9d367a3bbdf"}],"sha":"18878cadb5ab0ca6112d698989061231e391df83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commits/18878cadb5ab0ca6112d698989061231e391df83"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1402814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r","id":1402814,"login":"codebend3r","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MDI4MTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commits/1cee3e8f2a561f8e499d6393fb63f9d367a3bbdf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T00:39:21Z","email":"cj.rivas.dev@gmail.com","name":"CJ Rivas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T00:39:21Z","email":"cj.rivas.dev@gmail.com","name":"CJ Rivas"},"message":"Point the deployed world at the deployed jerry\n\nThe Netlify build never set JERRY_ORIGIN, so the address book fell\nthrough to its localhost:5103 default and world shipped that URL to\nproduction. Rick and morty are laid out on this origin by the build, so\nthey were unaffected; jerry is the one remote whose address has to come\nfrom outside the build, and it was the only one that failed to load.\n\nJerry''s own site already serves remoteEntry.js with the CORS headers\nworld needs, so the fix is the environment variable that was always\nmeant to carry the origin. The value has to match JERRY_ORIGIN in the\nguest repo''s netlify.toml, trailing slash included. Local dev is\nunchanged: unset still means jerry''s dev port.","tree":{"sha":"b147d5401f28922d9d9bc2b4fab622e47a222dd7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/git/trees/b147d5401f28922d9d9bc2b4fab622e47a222dd7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/git/commits/1cee3e8f2a561f8e499d6393fb63f9d367a3bbdf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1402814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r","id":1402814,"login":"codebend3r","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MDI4MTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commit/1cee3e8f2a561f8e499d6393fb63f9d367a3bbdf","node_id":"C_kwDOT4ChmdoAKDFjZWUzZThmMmE1NjFmOGU0OTlkNjM5M2ZiNjNmOWQzNjdhM2JiZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commit/ab6a4296353ff5a266a4a5628cae5b8bc002e9e5","sha":"ab6a4296353ff5a266a4a5628cae5b8bc002e9e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commits/ab6a4296353ff5a266a4a5628cae5b8bc002e9e5"}],"sha":"1cee3e8f2a561f8e499d6393fb63f9d367a3bbdf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commits/1cee3e8f2a561f8e499d6393fb63f9d367a3bbdf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1402814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r","id":1402814,"login":"codebend3r","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MDI4MTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commits/ab6a4296353ff5a266a4a5628cae5b8bc002e9e5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T00:30:29Z","email":"cj.rivas.dev@gmail.com","name":"CJ Rivas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T00:30:29Z","email":"cj.rivas.dev@gmail.com","name":"CJ Rivas"},"message":"Load jerry, a guest remote from another repo, into world\n\nJerry is built, served and versioned in micro-fe-prototype--guest. World\ntreats it like rick and morty: a remoteEntry.js URL, a /jerry prefix, and\nthe same props bag. The address book points at localhost:5103 unless\nJERRY_ORIGIN is set at build time, so a deployed world reaches a deployed\njerry through one environment variable. Jerry is not part of this repo''s\nbuild or Netlify layout, because it is not this repo''s to build.","tree":{"sha":"7ce41961b64c87f96758d201fd5296a8585c642b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/git/trees/7ce41961b64c87f96758d201fd5296a8585c642b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/git/commits/ab6a4296353ff5a266a4a5628cae5b8bc002e9e5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1402814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r","id":1402814,"login":"codebend3r","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MDI4MTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commit/ab6a4296353ff5a266a4a5628cae5b8bc002e9e5","node_id":"C_kwDOT4ChmdoAKGFiNmE0Mjk2MzUzZmY1YTI2NmE0YTU2MjhjYWU1YjhiYzAwMmU5ZTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commit/f3e387276bbc6657db61306f8849b0d5a18220c9","sha":"f3e387276bbc6657db61306f8849b0d5a18220c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commits/f3e387276bbc6657db61306f8849b0d5a18220c9"}],"sha":"ab6a4296353ff5a266a4a5628cae5b8bc002e9e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commits/ab6a4296353ff5a266a4a5628cae5b8bc002e9e5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1402814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r","id":1402814,"login":"codebend3r","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MDI4MTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commits/f3e387276bbc6657db61306f8849b0d5a18220c9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T22:09:22Z","email":"cj.rivas.dev@gmail.com","name":"CJ Rivas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T22:09:22Z","email":"cj.rivas.dev@gmail.com","name":"CJ Rivas"},"message":"Refactor into one micro frontend: world shell, rick and morty remotes\n\nRemove option 1, the comparison harness and the option 2 folders, and\nrebuild the workspace as a single system. World is the shell; rick and\nmorty are remotes it lazy loads over module federation the first time\ntheir route matches. Every app is on React 19 and routes with wouter.\nNothing is federated as shared: each app bundles its own React and\nwouter, and remotes expose mount(el, props).\n\nRouting is path based with three routers on one URL. World uses nested\nroutes for /rick and /morty and passes the prefix to each remote as a\nmount prop, which the remote''s own wouter uses as its base. Rick has two\nroutes (/, /lab) and morty three (/, /school, /inventory). Back, forward,\ndeep links and links inside a remote all work off the browser history.\n\nPorts are now 5100, 5101 and 5102. Deployed, the remotes sit under\n/apps/ so their folders never collide with world''s routes, and\nnetlify.toml gains SPA fallbacks for world and each standalone remote.\n\nDrop the probe bookkeeping that only existed to compare the two options,\nthe unused host mount prop, and CSS nothing renders any more. Document\nthe routing mechanism in docs/routing.md and link it from the README.","tree":{"sha":"c60a481f972980381017e5ca59609fe76c012796","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/git/trees/c60a481f972980381017e5ca59609fe76c012796"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/git/commits/f3e387276bbc6657db61306f8849b0d5a18220c9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1402814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r","id":1402814,"login":"codebend3r","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MDI4MTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commit/f3e387276bbc6657db61306f8849b0d5a18220c9","node_id":"C_kwDOT4ChmdoAKGYzZTM4NzI3NmJiYzY2NTdkYjYxMzA2Zjg4NDliMGQ1YTE4MjIwYzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commit/10e26bacb125a4187175885da797d051c42747d5","sha":"10e26bacb125a4187175885da797d051c42747d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commits/10e26bacb125a4187175885da797d051c42747d5"}],"sha":"f3e387276bbc6657db61306f8849b0d5a18220c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commits/f3e387276bbc6657db61306f8849b0d5a18220c9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1402814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r","id":1402814,"login":"codebend3r","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MDI4MTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commits/10e26bacb125a4187175885da797d051c42747d5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:44:18Z","email":"cj.rivas.dev@gmail.com","name":"CJ Rivas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T20:44:18Z","email":"cj.rivas.dev@gmail.com","name":"CJ Rivas"},"message":"Push a history entry per route change so back and forward work\n\nThe Shell wrote every route to the URL hash with replaceState, so three\nclicks through the nav left one history entry with its hash rewritten\nthree times. Back left the site instead of returning to the previous\nroute.\n\nIn-app navigation now pushes an entry. Route changes that arrive from\nthe URL itself, meaning the initial hash, a hand edited hash, and back\nor forward, already have an entry and are applied to the store without\npushing another one.\n\nA Shell embedded in the comparison harness keeps using replaceState.\nBoth iframes share the tab''s history, and two pushes per click would\nput the pair out of step on the first back press.","tree":{"sha":"124a453b50cf5ed08f6139270f7efbcba739440c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/git/trees/124a453b50cf5ed08f6139270f7efbcba739440c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/git/commits/10e26bacb125a4187175885da797d051c42747d5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1402814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r","id":1402814,"login":"codebend3r","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MDI4MTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commit/10e26bacb125a4187175885da797d051c42747d5","node_id":"C_kwDOT4ChmdoAKDEwZTI2YmFjYjEyNWE0MTg3MTc1ODg1ZGE3OTdkMDUxYzQyNzQ3ZDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commit/cabc6fa505b306c17b1e982e7fccf34da0f7ebfe","sha":"cabc6fa505b306c17b1e982e7fccf34da0f7ebfe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commits/cabc6fa505b306c17b1e982e7fccf34da0f7ebfe"}],"sha":"10e26bacb125a4187175885da797d051c42747d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commits/10e26bacb125a4187175885da797d051c42747d5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1402814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r","id":1402814,"login":"codebend3r","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MDI4MTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commits/cabc6fa505b306c17b1e982e7fccf34da0f7ebfe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T20:47:43Z","email":"cj.rivas.dev@gmail.com","name":"CJ Rivas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T20:47:43Z","email":"cj.rivas.dev@gmail.com","name":"CJ Rivas"},"message":"Note that pushing to main publishes the deployed copy\n\nThe Netlify site is connected to this repository with a read only deploy key,\nso `main` builds and publishes on push rather than needing a deploy run by\nhand. The build runs `bun run build:netlify` in Netlify''s image against the\n`BUN_VERSION` and `NODE_VERSION` pinned in `netlify.toml`.","tree":{"sha":"385163f4e3d31fa80e56b9c6974eb929ee0d8f9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/git/trees/385163f4e3d31fa80e56b9c6974eb929ee0d8f9a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/git/commits/cabc6fa505b306c17b1e982e7fccf34da0f7ebfe","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1402814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r","id":1402814,"login":"codebend3r","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MDI4MTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commit/cabc6fa505b306c17b1e982e7fccf34da0f7ebfe","node_id":"C_kwDOT4ChmdoAKGNhYmM2ZmE1MDViMzA2YzE3YjFlOTgyZTdmY2NmMzRkYTBmN2ViZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commit/f11c7545e92d062c5b1074a5649065fc66306778","sha":"f11c7545e92d062c5b1074a5649065fc66306778","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commits/f11c7545e92d062c5b1074a5649065fc66306778"}],"sha":"cabc6fa505b306c17b1e982e7fccf34da0f7ebfe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commits/cabc6fa505b306c17b1e982e7fccf34da0f7ebfe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1402814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r","id":1402814,"login":"codebend3r","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MDI4MTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commits/f11c7545e92d062c5b1074a5649065fc66306778/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T20:41:54Z","email":"cj.rivas.dev@gmail.com","name":"CJ Rivas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T20:41:54Z","email":"cj.rivas.dev@gmail.com","name":"CJ Rivas"},"message":"Deploy the prototype to Netlify, on one origin instead of seven\n\nLive at https://micro-fe-prototype.netlify.app. Locally the seven apps are\nseven origins on seven ports, which is the honest shape of a micro frontend\nsystem. A static host hands out one origin, so the deployed build gives each\napp its own path prefix on that single origin instead: the comparison harness\nat `/`, then `/option1/shell/`, `/option1/app1/`, `/option1/app2/` and the same\nthree under `/option2/`. Nothing about the architecture changes. Six\nindependent builds, Shells still fetching `remoteEntry.js` at runtime, remotes\nstill redeployable without the Shell. Only the addresses are different.\n\n* `scripts/deploy-target.ts` is the one place any app''s address is written\n  down. It holds two address books, and `MFE_TARGET=netlify` picks the\n  deployed one. Every vite config now reads its `base` and its remote entries\n  from it, so no port number is typed into a config anymore.\n* The addresses the UI prints on screen are injected through vite''s `define`\n  rather than hardcoded: the `app1 @ localhost:5011` pill in both Shells, the\n  harness iframe URLs and links, and the `federation({...})` sample on each\n  Overview tab, which now interpolates its entries and so stays true in either\n  target. `scripts/build-globals.d.ts` declares the injected constants.\n* `scripts/assemble-dist.mjs` stacks the seven `dist` folders into one\n  publishable `dist/`, and refuses to run against a build made without\n  `MFE_TARGET=netlify`, which would have localhost baked into it.\n* `netlify.toml` publishes that folder, pins Bun 1.3.14 and Node 22, and\n  redirects `/option1` and `/option2` to their Shells. Both Shells route on\n  the URL hash, so every deployed path is a real file and no SPA fallback rule\n  is needed.\n* `bun run build:netlify` runs the whole sequence. `bun run clean` now also\n  removes the assembled `dist/`, and `.netlify/` is ignored.\n\nTwo things the single origin changes, both cosmetic: the probe''s \"JavaScript\nby origin\" table collapses to one row, and `Timing-Allow-Origin` stops\nmattering because every script is same origin. The headers are still sent,\nbecause locally they are the only reason those numbers exist.\n\nVerified against the deployed site, not just the build output. Option 1 loads\n`app1` over federation with React copies still at 1 and the remote reporting\n`useSession() reached the Shell provider`. Option 2 runs 19.2.8 and 18.3.1 side\nby side with the remote reporting `store arrived as a mount prop`. The harness\nboots both Shells in iframes and telemetry flows back over `postMessage`. The\nlocal three origin workflow is unchanged: `bun run serve:option1` still serves\n5010 to 5012 and the probe still breaks the bytes down by port.","tree":{"sha":"ff1f59a927f093f8c5d6b80211935462f8a7f442","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/git/trees/ff1f59a927f093f8c5d6b80211935462f8a7f442"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/git/commits/f11c7545e92d062c5b1074a5649065fc66306778","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1402814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r","id":1402814,"login":"codebend3r","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MDI4MTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commit/f11c7545e92d062c5b1074a5649065fc66306778","node_id":"C_kwDOT4ChmdoAKGYxMWM3NTQ1ZTkyZDA2MmM1YjEwNzRhNTY0OTA2NWZjNjYzMDY3Nzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commit/f3f79e3bd3f0b82f61ad2cf25035910fe2ccbece","sha":"f3f79e3bd3f0b82f61ad2cf25035910fe2ccbece","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commits/f3f79e3bd3f0b82f61ad2cf25035910fe2ccbece"}],"sha":"f11c7545e92d062c5b1074a5649065fc66306778","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commits/f11c7545e92d062c5b1074a5649065fc66306778"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1402814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/codebend3r","id":1402814,"login":"codebend3r","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MDI4MTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codebend3r","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/commits/f3f79e3bd3f0b82f61ad2cf25035910fe2ccbece/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T18:53:34Z","email":"cj.rivas.dev@gmail.com","name":"CJ Rivas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T18:53:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Move the workspace from pnpm to Bun (#2)\n\nBun replaces pnpm as both the package manager and the script runner. Nothing\nabout the two integration strategies changes; this is the toolchain underneath\nthem. Node still executes Vite, because `bun run` honours the `#!/usr/bin/env\nnode` shebang on Vite''s binary, so builds and dev servers behave exactly as\nbefore.\n\n* The workspace list moves from `pnpm-workspace.yaml` into the `workspaces`\n  field of the root `package.json`, and `pnpm-workspace.yaml` and\n  `pnpm-lock.yaml` are deleted in favour of `bun.lock`.\n* `onlyBuiltDependencies` becomes `trustedDependencies`, still just `esbuild`,\n  which needs its postinstall to fetch the platform binary Vite depends on.\n* `packageManager: pnpm@10` gives way to `engines.bun >= 1.2.0`.\n* Every root script switches to Bun. `pnpm --filter \"@o1/*\" build` becomes\n  `bun run --filter \"@o1/*\" build`, and the per app commands `concurrently`\n  drives become `bun run --cwd <dir> <script>`. The flag has to sit after\n  `run`; `bun --cwd <dir> run <script>` prints the help instead.\n* `concurrently` stays, so `dev` and `serve` keep their named, coloured\n  prefixes across seven processes.\n\nBun installs with the isolated linker, which this repo depends on more than\nmost: Option 2''s `app1` has to genuinely resolve React 18 while every other app\nresolves React 19, rather than one hoisted copy winning. Verified after the\nswitch, with all seven servers up on a clean build.\n\n`scripts/ports.mjs` now runs under Bun and recognises `bun` alongside `node` as\na listener it owns, so a stack started with `bun run --bun` can still be stopped\nby `bun run stop`. Its messages point at `bun run stop` and `bun run start`.\n\nThe README gains an \"Installing Bun\" section covering the shell installer,\nHomebrew, npm and PowerShell, plus a note on why `bun run build` is spelled out\nin full: `build` is one of Bun''s own subcommands, so `bun build` would fire the\nbundler instead of this repo''s build script. Every remaining `pnpm` reference\nis updated.","tree":{"sha":"f67a5012efc849076dac3b956193e0667b88cff8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/git/trees/f67a5012efc849076dac3b956193e0667b88cff8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codebend3r/micro-fe-prototype/git/commits/f3f79e3bd3f0b82f61ad2cf25035910fe2ccbece","verification":{"payload":"tree f67a5012efc849076dac3b956193e0667b88cff8\nparent fd31ffa416f270f8d65189ffd7e8c2439853ef69\nauthor CJ Rivas <cj.rivas.dev@gmail.com> 1786733614 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786733614 -0400\n\nMove the workspace from pnpm to Bun (#2)\n\nBun replaces pnpm as both the package manager and the script runner. Nothing\nabout the two integration strategies changes; this is the toolchain underneath\nthem. Node still executes Vite, because `bun run` honours the `#!/usr/bin/env\nnode` shebang on Vite''s binary, so builds and dev servers behave exactly as\nbefore.\n\n* The workspace list moves from `pnpm-workspace.yaml` into the `workspaces`\n  field of the root `package.json`, and `pnpm-workspace.yaml` and\n  `pnpm-lock.yaml` are deleted in favour of `bun.lock`.\n* `onlyBuiltDependencies` becomes `trustedDependencies`, still just `esbuild`,\n  which needs its postinstall to fetch the platform binary Vite depends on.\n* `packageManager: pnpm@10` gives way to `engines.bun >= 1.2.0`.\n* Every root script switches to Bun. `pnpm --filter \"@o1/*\" build` becomes\n  `bun run --filter \"@o1/*\" build`, and the per app commands `concurrently`\n  drives become `bun run --cwd <dir> <script>`. The flag has to sit after\n  `run`; `bun --cwd <dir> run <script>` prints the help instead.\n* `concurrently` stays, so `dev` and `serve` keep their named, coloured\n  prefixes across seven processes.\n\nBun installs with the isolated linker, which this repo depends on more than\nmost: Option 2''s `app1` has to genuinely resolve React 18 while every other app\nresolves React 19, rather than one hoisted copy winning. Verified after the\nswitch, with all seven servers up on a clean build.\n\n`scripts/ports.mjs` now runs under Bun and recognises `bun` alongside `node` as\na listener it owns, so a stack started with `bun run --bun` can still be stopped\nby `bun run stop`. Its messages point at `bun run stop` and `bun run start`.\n\nThe README gains an \"Installing Bun\" section covering the shell installer,\nHomebrew, npm and PowerShell, plus a note on why `bun run build` is spelled out\nin full: `build` is one of Bun''s own subcommands, so `bun build` would fire the\nbundler instead of this repo''s build script. Every remaining `pnpm` reference\nis updated.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqf2QuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/nsQAIDnAXM/WqY06ByjZ/k27GeE\njuon4fi6HEUZ6mVWifr1sf8JkdSgIzSmtuNOtB4Fs8zGDQha9JFX8sO6IQ8MuGPR\nIAXMuq3rrYMcIvBkyUNuxSLsvTLn7QiPrlXtj4/Z3JUKuQ2vis/wzu2DW9c1twbj\nsfMNvttIwgd