https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b","id":43937419,"login":"ramvignesh-b","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzOTM3NDE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commits/7b25d189deb2cbe768dbb4f1ba4e837e9f571901/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T11:07:41Z","email":"github@infra.iamatom.fyi","name":"ramvignesh-b"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T11:25:03Z","email":"github@infra.iamatom.fyi","name":"RamVignesh B"},"message":"feat(console): create a Link from the Fleet header\n\nA \"New link\" action opens /links/new, a form component over the eight\nLink fields validated by the shared linkCreateSchema. One whole-value\nvalidator, not one per control; a client-side failure sets no request\nissued. issueFor() is the one adapter that puts a FieldIssue[] onto a\ncontrol, reused for both the client-side safeParse result and a Server\nVALIDATION_FAILED/LINK_NAME_TAKEN envelope, so a name conflict lands on\nthe same name control with operatorMessageFor()''s copy rather than the\nServer''s diagnostic message. A successful create navigates to the new\nLink''s detail view.\n\noperatorMessageFor is an exhaustive switch on ApiErrorCode, guarded by\nnoImplicitReturns the same way LinksController.create''s own switch is.\n\nForm state is signals throughout, no @angular/forms.","tree":{"sha":"fd77710569a77dc91a94e074a732cac6a61c7e03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/git/trees/fd77710569a77dc91a94e074a732cac6a61c7e03"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/git/commits/7b25d189deb2cbe768dbb4f1ba4e837e9f571901","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43937419?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b","id":43937419,"login":"ramvignesh-b","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzOTM3NDE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commit/7b25d189deb2cbe768dbb4f1ba4e837e9f571901","node_id":"C_kwDOT4pnL9oAKDdiMjVkMTg5ZGViMmNiZTc2OGRiYjRmMWJhNGU4MzdlOWY1NzE5MDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commit/ba44edf668b7ee8cdeb17f90441769db0b480a73","sha":"ba44edf668b7ee8cdeb17f90441769db0b480a73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commits/ba44edf668b7ee8cdeb17f90441769db0b480a73"}],"sha":"7b25d189deb2cbe768dbb4f1ba4e837e9f571901","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commits/7b25d189deb2cbe768dbb4f1ba4e837e9f571901"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43937419?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b","id":43937419,"login":"ramvignesh-b","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzOTM3NDE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commits/ba44edf668b7ee8cdeb17f90441769db0b480a73/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T10:22:30Z","email":"github@infra.iamatom.fyi","name":"ramvignesh-b"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T10:26:25Z","email":"github@infra.iamatom.fyi","name":"RamVignesh B"},"message":"refactor(console): isolate link detail integration tests to eliminate complexity warning\n\nA single end-to-end integration test in `link-detail.spec.ts` bundled five\ndistinct assertions—navigation, REST/SSE overlap deduplication, sparkline\ngap threshold detection, 300-sample ring buffer capping, and route teardown/\nre-entry refetching—into a sequential 90-line block. The concatenation,\ncombined with defensive optional-chaining assertions (`path?.match(...)`),\npushed cyclomatic complexity to 15 against ESLint''s configured threshold of 10.\n\nSplits the monolithic test into five independent, focused scenario blocks with\nisolated test fixtures, and extracts `pointCount` and `subpathCount` helpers to\ncentralize SVG path segment inspections. Each behavior now runs and fails\nindependently with direct diagnostic locality.\n\nVerification:\n- apps/console: 9/9 link-detail tests green\n- ESLint: zero warnings or errors with --max-warnings 0\n- Workspace verification: 15/15 projects passing lint, test, and build\n\nRefs #34","tree":{"sha":"fbe3a01b3db7725edd6e05685e46e73cdc2f4581","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/git/trees/fbe3a01b3db7725edd6e05685e46e73cdc2f4581"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/git/commits/ba44edf668b7ee8cdeb17f90441769db0b480a73","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43937419?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b","id":43937419,"login":"ramvignesh-b","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzOTM3NDE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commit/ba44edf668b7ee8cdeb17f90441769db0b480a73","node_id":"C_kwDOT4pnL9oAKGJhNDRlZGY2NjhiN2VlOGNkZWIxN2Y5MDQ0MTc2OWRiMGI0ODBhNzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commit/6621b5c9f422b14b9fbdceecef58170a985d77f8","sha":"6621b5c9f422b14b9fbdceecef58170a985d77f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commits/6621b5c9f422b14b9fbdceecef58170a985d77f8"}],"sha":"ba44edf668b7ee8cdeb17f90441769db0b480a73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commits/ba44edf668b7ee8cdeb17f90441769db0b480a73"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43937419?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b","id":43937419,"login":"ramvignesh-b","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzOTM3NDE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commits/6621b5c9f422b14b9fbdceecef58170a985d77f8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T09:26:58Z","email":"github@infra.iamatom.fyi","name":"ramvignesh-b"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T10:26:25Z","email":"github@infra.iamatom.fyi","name":"RamVignesh B"},"message":"feat(console): render link detail, live telemetry, and sparkline history\n\nIntroduce the Link detail screen under `/links/:id`, displaying its\ncomplete radio configuration, live status, its latest Telemetry Sample,\nand a hand-rolled SVG sparkline charting Throughput over the last five\nminutes against the Capacity it is judged by.\n\nHistory is fetched once upon entering the route over REST — naming the\nfive-minute window explicitly rather than relying on the Server''s default,\nso the window the heading promises is one the Console actually asked for —\nand continuously updated from live SSE telemetry frames without polling.\nSamples merge and deduplicate on timestamp, unique by construction at one\nSample per Link per second. To keep a break in transmission visible rather\nthan interpolated, the path builder emits a new move (''M'') command whenever\nconsecutive Samples are more than two Ticks apart: one missed Tick is the\njitter of a 1 Hz producer, two is telemetry that stopped arriving.\n\nThe Y axis tops out a quarter above Capacity rather than at it, so the\nCapacity reference line is drawn inside the viewBox instead of half-clipped\non its edge, and a Link running over its provisioned ceiling looks different\nfrom one sitting exactly on it.\n\nThe buffer is capped at 300 Samples, matching the server-side ring buffer\nbound, and capped on write rather than on read so the map cannot hold more\nthan the chart shows. ADR-0010 records this as the third site of that number\nand keeps the three hand-coupled deliberately. History state is scoped to the\nroute injector via LinkHistory, structurally releasing memory when the\noperator navigates away.\n\nOnly a 404 renders not-found. Every other failure — offline, a timeout, a\n502 — is a Transport Failure in CONTEXT.md''s terms and says the Server did\nnot answer, because a dropped connection is not evidence of a deletion.\nNothing paints until the Server has answered, even when the store already\nholds the Link, since the store cannot distinguish deleted from not yet\nstreamed. After that answer the store takes over for liveness. A failed\nwindow fetch says so rather than leaving an empty chart, which would read\nas this Link having reported nothing.\n\nVerification:\n- libs/console/ui: unit tests for buildSparklinePath and Sparkline, covering\n  the gap threshold at its boundary and the capacity line''s position\n- libs/console/feature-link-detail: unit tests for LinkHistory, including a\n  Sample already in the store when the route opened\n- apps/console: end-to-end integration tests asserting deduplication across\n  overlapping windows, gap breaks in SVG paths, 300-sample capping, refetch\n  on re-entry, and not-found held apart from the Server not answering\n- Workspace verification: 15/15 projects passing lint, typecheck, test, and\n  production build; Console initial bundle 604 kB against a 650 kB warning\n\nCloses #34","tree":{"sha":"341f882ea0ae7bbe8f74b74d0f92449d8f61c067","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/git/trees/341f882ea0ae7bbe8f74b74d0f92449d8f61c067"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/git/commits/6621b5c9f422b14b9fbdceecef58170a985d77f8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43937419?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b","id":43937419,"login":"ramvignesh-b","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzOTM3NDE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commit/6621b5c9f422b14b9fbdceecef58170a985d77f8","node_id":"C_kwDOT4pnL9oAKDY2MjFiNWM5ZjQyMmIxNGI5ZmJkY2VlY2VmNTgxNzBhOTg1ZDc3Zjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commit/fc8c234ac7cc5b9ffcaec8bbeedf5520eaba7e7c","sha":"fc8c234ac7cc5b9ffcaec8bbeedf5520eaba7e7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commits/fc8c234ac7cc5b9ffcaec8bbeedf5520eaba7e7c"}],"sha":"6621b5c9f422b14b9fbdceecef58170a985d77f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commits/6621b5c9f422b14b9fbdceecef58170a985d77f8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43937419?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b","id":43937419,"login":"ramvignesh-b","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzOTM3NDE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commits/fc8c234ac7cc5b9ffcaec8bbeedf5520eaba7e7c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T08:41:56Z","email":"github@infra.iamatom.fyi","name":"ramvignesh-b"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T09:02:03Z","email":"github@infra.iamatom.fyi","name":"RamVignesh B"},"message":"fix(console): stop two quick filter changes from racing each other\n\nCode review on ticket 32 found that `queryParamsHandling: ''merge''`\nreads `Router.currentUrlTree`, which only updates once a navigation\nfinishes — not when `navigate()` is called. Two `FleetFilterBar`\noutputs firing back to back (a future \"reset filters\" control,\nscripted interaction, or just two clicks the router hasn''t caught up\nwith yet) both merged against the same stale tree, and the router\nkeeps the later of two overlapping navigations, so the first control''s\nchange silently vanished from the URL. `updateQuery` now chains every\n`navigate()` call onto a `pendingNavigation` promise, so the second\ncall''s merge always reads the first''s committed result. Confirmed by\nmutation: reverting the chain turns `sort`+`dir` fired without an\nintervening tick back into a dropped `sort`, which the test — now\nfiring both without an await between them — catches.\n\nTwo smaller findings from the same pass: `query` and the fallback\n`effect` each ran their own `linkListQuerySchema.safeParse` on an\nidentically-built raw object, two copies of \"is this invalid\" a future\nedit could bring out of step — collapsed into one `parsedQuery`\ncomputed both read. And `FleetFilterBar`''s sort-key labels were a\nhand-typed array never checked against `linkSortKeySchema`, so a new\nsort key could ship without a compile error and just be missing from\nthe dropdown — now `linkSortKeySchema.options` drives the list and a\n`Record<LinkSortKey, string>` forces the label in at compile time.\n\nVerification: `nx run-many -t test lint typecheck build`, 15 projects\ngreen.\n\nCloses #33","tree":{"sha":"e8969cb9f61d50138f79da3dfeb37645d355f90d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/git/trees/e8969cb9f61d50138f79da3dfeb37645d355f90d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/git/commits/fc8c234ac7cc5b9ffcaec8bbeedf5520eaba7e7c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43937419?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b","id":43937419,"login":"ramvignesh-b","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzOTM3NDE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commit/fc8c234ac7cc5b9ffcaec8bbeedf5520eaba7e7c","node_id":"C_kwDOT4pnL9oAKGZjOGMyMzRhYzdjYzViOWZmY2FlYzhiYmVlZGY1NTIwZWFiYTdlN2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commit/85ef3afbb74a5741f302ebbc11b0baea22bd18af","sha":"85ef3afbb74a5741f302ebbc11b0baea22bd18af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commits/85ef3afbb74a5741f302ebbc11b0baea22bd18af"}],"sha":"fc8c234ac7cc5b9ffcaec8bbeedf5520eaba7e7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commits/fc8c234ac7cc5b9ffcaec8bbeedf5520eaba7e7c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43937419?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b","id":43937419,"login":"ramvignesh-b","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzOTM3NDE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commits/85ef3afbb74a5741f302ebbc11b0baea22bd18af/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T08:41:34Z","email":"github@infra.iamatom.fyi","name":"ramvignesh-b"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T09:02:03Z","email":"github@infra.iamatom.fyi","name":"RamVignesh B"},"message":"refactor(domain): share the band/q filter the same way sortLinks is shared\n\nTicket 32''s code review caught the follow-on to the sortLinks move:\n`applyListQuery`''s band-exact/q-substring filter was a line-for-line\ncopy of `InMemoryLinkRepository.findAll`''s, not a shared function — the\nsame drift risk the sortLinks move exists to prevent, left unclosed for\nfiltering. `matchesBandAndQuery` moves that predicate into\n`shared/domain`; the repository and `applyListQuery` both call it\ninstead of each keeping its own copy.\n\nVerification: `nx run-many -t test lint -p shared-domain\nserver-links-data-access console-data-access`, 123, 19 and 7 tests\ngreen.\n\nRefs #33","tree":{"sha":"2587b17d482653bc50cd713e851be4112a3c5057","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/git/trees/2587b17d482653bc50cd713e851be4112a3c5057"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/git/commits/85ef3afbb74a5741f302ebbc11b0baea22bd18af","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43937419?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b","id":43937419,"login":"ramvignesh-b","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzOTM3NDE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commit/85ef3afbb74a5741f302ebbc11b0baea22bd18af","node_id":"C_kwDOT4pnL9oAKDg1ZWYzYWZiYjc0YTU3NDFmMzAyZWJiYzExYjBiYWVhMjJiZDE4YWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commit/1d044a841649fd1fa0b011e829ed410316e31474","sha":"1d044a841649fd1fa0b011e829ed410316e31474","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commits/1d044a841649fd1fa0b011e829ed410316e31474"}],"sha":"85ef3afbb74a5741f302ebbc11b0baea22bd18af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commits/85ef3afbb74a5741f302ebbc11b0baea22bd18af"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43937419?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b","id":43937419,"login":"ramvignesh-b","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzOTM3NDE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commits/1d044a841649fd1fa0b011e829ed410316e31474/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T08:26:52Z","email":"github@infra.iamatom.fyi","name":"ramvignesh-b"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T09:02:03Z","email":"github@infra.iamatom.fyi","name":"RamVignesh B"},"message":"feat(console): filter and sort the Fleet, with the URL as the state\n\nAn operator narrows the Fleet by Status, Band or free text across\nname and Sites, sorts by name, Capacity, Status or Throughput in\neither direction, and every choice lives in the query string — so the\nview is shareable by copying the address bar and survives a reload\nuntouched.\n\n`FleetPage` reads the five parameters as router-bound inputs\n(`withComponentInputBinding`, added to `provideRouter`) rather than a\nsubscription it would have to keep in step, and re-parses them with\n`linkListQuerySchema` — the same schema `LinkListQueryDto` wraps for\nthe Server''s validation pipe. `applyListQuery` (`console/data-access`)\nfilters and sorts the store with that parsed query, using the shared\n`sortLinks`, so the two orderings, ties included, cannot drift apart.\nIt runs as a `computed`, so a Link that transitions to `degraded` on a\nlater Tick enters a `degraded`-only view immediately: there is no\nrefetch to trigger, because the Console was never asking the Server to\nfilter in the first place. The KPI header keeps reading\n`FleetStore.summary()` — the whole-Fleet Summary, untouched by the\nfilter — so narrowing the list can never hide a `down` Link from the\ncounts above it.\n\nA query string the schema rejects — a mistyped `status`, an unknown\n`sort` key — is not shown as an error: an `effect` resolves it to the\ndefaults and rewrites the URL with `replaceUrl: true`, the one\ndeliberate exception to this Console surfacing every failure, because\na mistyped address is not an action the operator took.\n\n`FleetFilterBar` (`console/ui`) is the presentational control strip —\nfive inputs, five outputs, no store and no router — built from the\nsame `linkStatusKindSchema`/`bandSchema` option lists the wire\ncontract already defines, so a Band or Status added there needs no\nsecond edit here.\n\nThe app-level test harness (`FakeEventSource`, `bootConsole`, `screen`,\n`finish`) moves out of `live-fleet.spec.ts` into\n`apps/console/src/app/testing/console-harness.ts` so the new spec\ndoesn''t duplicate it; `bootConsole` now takes the initial route so a\ntest can boot straight into a query string. That file is excluded from\n`tsconfig.app.json` — it calls vitest''s `expect`, which only the spec\n`tsconfig` declares the types for, and it must not ship in the\nproduction bundle regardless.\n\nVerification: `nx run-many -t test lint typecheck build`, 15 projects\ngreen. The new app-level test covers a filtered, sorted URL rendering\nthe right rows in the right order; four separate control changes each\nwriting the URL; a Link crossing into a `degraded`-only view on a\nlater Tick with no refetch (`HttpTestingController.verify()` in\n`finish()` is what proves that); and an unparseable query string\nfalling back and rewriting rather than erroring, in a second boot in\nthe same test. Checked by mutation: gutting the fallback `effect` to a\nno-op turned the \"not.toContain(''bogus'')\" assertion red.\n\nCloses #33","tree":{"sha":"fc4b7b565fc79393576f197854068c28fc8e140c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/git/trees/fc4b7b565fc79393576f197854068c28fc8e140c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/git/commits/1d044a841649fd1fa0b011e829ed410316e31474","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43937419?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b","id":43937419,"login":"ramvignesh-b","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzOTM3NDE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commit/1d044a841649fd1fa0b011e829ed410316e31474","node_id":"C_kwDOT4pnL9oAKDFkMDQ0YTg0MTY0OWZkMWZhMGIwMTFlODI5ZWQ0MTAzMTZlMzE0NzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commit/702ffdd4b5c1f9f959bcd160e1e6ad786bd3ed17","sha":"702ffdd4b5c1f9f959bcd160e1e6ad786bd3ed17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commits/702ffdd4b5c1f9f959bcd160e1e6ad786bd3ed17"}],"sha":"1d044a841649fd1fa0b011e829ed410316e31474","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commits/1d044a841649fd1fa0b011e829ed410316e31474"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43937419?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b","id":43937419,"login":"ramvignesh-b","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzOTM3NDE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commits/702ffdd4b5c1f9f959bcd160e1e6ad786bd3ed17/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T08:26:12Z","email":"github@infra.iamatom.fyi","name":"ramvignesh-b"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T09:02:03Z","email":"github@infra.iamatom.fyi","name":"RamVignesh B"},"message":"refactor(domain): give sortLinks a home both platforms can reach\n\nTicket 32 needs the Console''s filtered view to tie-break exactly the\nway `GET /api/links` does, and the only way to guarantee that is to\nrun the same comparator rather than two that started identical and\ndrifted. `sortLinks` lived in `server/links-api`, which the platform\nfirewall puts off-limits to the Console — `platform:console` can only\nreach `platform:console` and `platform:shared` — so it moves into\n`shared/domain`, the one library both sides are already allowed to\nimport. The function and its tie-break logic are unchanged; only the\nimport paths move, in `links.controller.ts` and its own spec.\n\nVerification: `nx run-many -t test lint -p shared-domain server-links-api`,\n118 and 49 tests green.\n\nRefs #33","tree":{"sha":"5d7ac2055342805a6e1ff8663628ed389f13ddc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/git/trees/5d7ac2055342805a6e1ff8663628ed389f13ddc3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/git/commits/702ffdd4b5c1f9f959bcd160e1e6ad786bd3ed17","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43937419?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b","id":43937419,"login":"ramvignesh-b","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzOTM3NDE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramvignesh-b","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commit/702ffdd4b5c1f9f959bcd160e1e6ad786bd3ed17","node_id":"C_kwDOT4pnL9oAKDcwMmZmZGQ0YjVjMWY5Zjk1OWJjZDE2MGUxZTZhZDc4NmJkM2VkMTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commit/0b9d2d2d0ed8d17cb1d9bd57edd895299fdbba32","sha":"0b9d2d2d0ed8d17cb1d9bd57edd895299fdbba32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ramvignesh-b/linkops/commits/0b9d2d2d0ed8d17cb1d9bd57edd895299fdbba32"}],"sha":"702ffdd4b5c1f9f959bcd160e1e6ad786bd3ed17","url":"https://api