"login":"Tarun1515","providerType":"User"},"email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:13:06.774Z","repositoryId":1334633698,"sha":"a54b6d6d60ff8e89539825d368b581e235259e74"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"Tarun1515","providerType":"User"},"email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-08T18:32:41Z","committedDate":"2026-08-08T18:32:41Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"Tarun1515","providerType":"User"},"email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:13:06.774Z","repositoryId":1334633698,"sha":"f4f81acd72c83f854aa9da0925f22b83cd20540e"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"Tarun1515","providerType":"User"},"email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-08T16:50:57Z","committedDate":"2026-08-08T16:50:57Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"Tarun1515","providerType":"User"},"email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:13:06.774Z","repositoryId":1334633698,"sha":"de68432f99515a0f844ad570c4285bb449835095"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:13:06.774Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commits/1fe0128047afc30c259d2200f8524b933ad7598a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T14:27:51Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T14:27:51Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"5B: the filter strip moves into the system, and actionLink starts working\n\nPhase 5B needed six new screens across two apps. The cheapest route was to\ncopy the chrome into each of them, which is exactly the drift G27 records —\nthree private copies of `.tabs` and `.banner` that already disagree with each\nother in small ways. So the new screens take the system''s classes, and the\none pattern that genuinely belongs to more than one app moved into it.\n\n`.page__toolbar` already existed with no children. The 1D applicants mockup\nhad designed the strip and hand-rolled its parts as `.filters__*`; 5B needed\nthe same strip on the school''s applicants, the teacher''s job browse and the\nteacher''s applications. The children live here now, defined once.\n\n🔴 `.tabs` deliberately did NOT move, and that is the more interesting half.\nIts three copies differ — margin-bottom, overflow-x, the background and border\nresets, white-space — and a global version would leak properties into screens\nthat omit them on purpose. Promoting it mid-phase would have been a visual\nchange to three shipped screens in exchange for tidiness. So the teacher''s\napplications list uses the toolbar idiom instead of growing a fourth copy, and\nG27 is neither larger nor smaller than it was.\n\n🔴 ui-empty-state''s `actionLink` was not an input, and three shipped buttons\ndid nothing because of it. It has been written on this component since 4B — the\njobs list''s empty state and both of the school dashboard''s — as a plain\nattribute. Angular set it on the host element and dropped it: the button\nrendered, the click emitted `action`, nobody was listening. \"Post a job\" was\ninert for four weeks.\n\nIt could not have been caught by a type error either. `[actionLink]=\"…\"` would\nhave failed the build on day one; `actionLink=\"…\"` is legal HTML and compiles\nhappily. That is the whole bug, and it is why the fix is an input rather than\nthree rewritten call sites. When set, the action renders as an anchor, so\nmiddle-click and \"open in new tab\" work — a router navigate() behind a button\ntakes both away. It is ignored while actionDisabled is true, because a \"not\nyet\" action must not be followable.\n\nRESUME_REQUIRED and JOB_EXPIRED join COMPONENT_RENDERED_CODES: the teacher''s\napply panel renders both in place, because each has a next step a toast cannot\ncarry — one links to the resume section, the other replaces the button with the\ndate applications closed. Deliberately only those two of the six application\ncodes; listing a code nothing renders is how a refusal becomes silence.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e80253217e81d608fbde10ab74bf787f351bc209","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/git/trees/e80253217e81d608fbde10ab74bf787f351bc209"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/git/commits/1fe0128047afc30c259d2200f8524b933ad7598a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commit/1fe0128047afc30c259d2200f8524b933ad7598a","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zk4toAKDFmZTAxMjgwNDdhZmMzMGMyNTlkMjIwMGY4NTI0YjkzM2FkNzU5OGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commit/2b21e24bc133902fac6e58290067cafc13dd7325","sha":"2b21e24bc133902fac6e58290067cafc13dd7325","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commits/2b21e24bc133902fac6e58290067cafc13dd7325"}],"sha":"1fe0128047afc30c259d2200f8524b933ad7598a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commits/1fe0128047afc30c259d2200f8524b933ad7598a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commits/2b21e24bc133902fac6e58290067cafc13dd7325/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T09:14:21Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T09:14:21Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"Master keys: employment type, job status, and the three ledger masters\n\nThe client half of these already existed for employment type and job\nstatus; the server could not answer them until PRE-5. Added the three\nledger keys alongside, and a note on which database answers — and why\nthat is invisible to every caller.\n\n⚠️ If a component ever needs to know which database a master came from,\nthe fix belongs on the server, not in a branch here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"424b435084ec908724d2454b8dd177ca1b2d5cf7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/git/trees/424b435084ec908724d2454b8dd177ca1b2d5cf7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/git/commits/2b21e24bc133902fac6e58290067cafc13dd7325","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commit/2b21e24bc133902fac6e58290067cafc13dd7325","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zk4toAKDJiMjFlMjRiYzEzMzkwMmZhYzZlNTgyOTAwNjdjYWZjMTNkZDczMjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commit/1213d3c1d90d975c2b61b276facd96121710d7f2","sha":"1213d3c1d90d975c2b61b276facd96121710d7f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commits/1213d3c1d90d975c2b61b276facd96121710d7f2"}],"sha":"2b21e24bc133902fac6e58290067cafc13dd7325","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commits/2b21e24bc133902fac6e58290067cafc13dd7325"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commits/1213d3c1d90d975c2b61b276facd96121710d7f2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T12:30:25Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T12:30:25Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"Error interceptor: do not toast codes a component renders itself\n\nOne refusal produced two messages — the interceptor''s (the server''s\nsentence) and the screen''s (the fuller one, with when the allowance\nresets and that the job is safe as a draft). The verification printed the\ntoast text, so it was visible rather than merely present.\n\nThe reasoning already existed one line above: VALIDATION_FAILED skips the\ntoast because \"field-level errors belong on the form controls, not in a\ntoast that covers them up\". The same rule covers any code a component\nrenders — whoever says it best says it once, and for a quota refusal that\nis the screen.\n\nCOMPONENT_RENDERED_CODES, applied in both the 400 and the 403 branch.\nFEATURE_DISABLED arrives as a 403 and the generic \"you do not have\npermission\" would be actively misleading for it: it is an operator\ndecision, not a permission.\n\n🔴 Adding a code to that set is a promise that some component renders it.\nAn unhandled code there would fail silently, which is the one thing this\ninterceptor exists to prevent — so the entry and its handler belong in\nthe same change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f5246a34e8a73091f6ae15986fba08dff0a0211f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/git/trees/f5246a34e8a73091f6ae15986fba08dff0a0211f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/git/commits/1213d3c1d90d975c2b61b276facd96121710d7f2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commit/1213d3c1d90d975c2b61b276facd96121710d7f2","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zk4toAKDEyMTNkM2MxZDkwZDk3NWMyYjYxYjI3NmZhY2Q5NjEyMTcxMGQ3ZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commit/f942dd1ce324c1cd4977fa362bd7422fca84c44e","sha":"f942dd1ce324c1cd4977fa362bd7422fca84c44e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commits/f942dd1ce324c1cd4977fa362bd7422fca84c44e"}],"sha":"1213d3c1d90d975c2b61b276facd96121710d7f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commits/1213d3c1d90d975c2b61b276facd96121710d7f2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commits/f942dd1ce324c1cd4977fa362bd7422fca84c44e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T13:19:43Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T13:19:43Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"Phase 3I — ui-empty-state can show a disabled action and a \"when\"\n\nFor an area that does not exist yet: the action shows where the feature will be,\nand the note says when it arrives.\n\n🔴 \"Not yet\" only, never \"not allowed\". Everywhere else a disabled control is\nthe wrong answer — the head office has no Remove button and the team''s owner row\nhas no controls at all, because a greyed button reads as broken and gets clicked\nanyway. An action that does not EXIST is the one case worth showing, and the\ncomment on actionDisabled draws that line so nobody reaches for it to say \"you\nmay not do that\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0e3a86d683cf9600a7d3d28f7ab29d1b3ddaa356","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/git/trees/0e3a86d683cf9600a7d3d28f7ab29d1b3ddaa356"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/git/commits/f942dd1ce324c1cd4977fa362bd7422fca84c44e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commit/f942dd1ce324c1cd4977fa362bd7422fca84c44e","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zk4toAKGY5NDJkZDFjZTMyNGMxY2Q0OTc3ZmEzNjJiZDc0MjJmY2E4NGM0NGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commit/c6d067a49f7c516414a277b2ffaf843f52c15d23","sha":"c6d067a49f7c516414a277b2ffaf843f52c15d23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commits/c6d067a49f7c516414a277b2ffaf843f52c15d23"}],"sha":"f942dd1ce324c1cd4977fa362bd7422fca84c44e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commits/f942dd1ce324c1cd4977fa362bd7422fca84c44e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commits/c6d067a49f7c516414a277b2ffaf843f52c15d23/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T12:41:05Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T12:41:05Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"Phase 3H — rebuild ui-multi-select, and lift the section-save styles\n\nFive sections of the teacher profile depend on this one control, so every flaw\nin it was multiplied by five. Four were wrong, and none of them was visible by\nlooking:\n\nNested interactive elements. The chips'' remove buttons and the clear button\nlived inside the trigger <button> — invalid HTML, and in practice a screen\nreader reads the lot as one control while Space on a chip activates the button\nit sits in. Chips are siblings now, each a real button with its own name.\n\nNo keyboard navigation. Options were divs with tabindex=0, so the fortieth\nsubject was forty Tab presses away. Arrow keys move an active option with\naria-activedescendant; Enter toggles, Escape closes and returns focus.\n\nIt never closed. Only Escape closed the panel, so on a form with five of them\ntwo could be open at once, overlapping the next field.\n\nTwenty selections broke the layout. Chips inside the trigger inflated it into a\nwall of pills. The trigger summarises now — \"6 subjects selected\" — and the\nchips wrap underneath, where there can be as many as somebody likes.\n\nAlso: .save-note, .conflict, .note and .card-empty move here from the school and\nteacher profiles, where they had been written twice identically. Section-level\nsave is the house pattern for long forms now, and every one needs the same\nvocabulary: it saved, it clashed, or there is something to explain.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fe1a153c589e48bc23894f8b7f75f9227a6ec323","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/git/trees/fe1a153c589e48bc23894f8b7f75f9227a6ec323"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/git/commits/c6d067a49f7c516414a277b2ffaf843f52c15d23","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commit/c6d067a49f7c516414a277b2ffaf843f52c15d23","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zk4toAKGM2ZDA2N2E0OWY3YzUxNjQxNGEyNzdiMmZmYWY4NDNmNTJjMTVkMjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commit/e9c26181bf99ff92f2114baba128e8147ba6722b","sha":"e9c26181bf99ff92f2114baba128e8147ba6722b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commits/e9c26181bf99ff92f2114baba128e8147ba6722b"}],"sha":"c6d067a49f7c516414a277b2ffaf843f52c15d23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commits/c6d067a49f7c516414a277b2ffaf843f52c15d23"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commits/e9c26181bf99ff92f2114baba128e8147ba6722b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T11:59:18Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T11:59:18Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"Phase 3F — menu hideRoutes, unsavedChangesGuard, a compact control\n\nhideRoutes lets an app hide a route the SERVER permitted but its own data makes\nmeaningless — a single-campus school being shown a Campuses screen it can only\never have one row in. jp_sso issues the menu and has never heard of GroupType,\nso the app that does know has to be able to say so. Presentation, not\nprotection: the route guard still does that.\n\nunsavedChangesGuard uses the native confirm() on purpose. A router guard has to\nanswer synchronously to cancel a navigation already in flight, including the\nbrowser''s back button — a styled dialog that resolves afterwards is asking\nabout a page the user has already left.\n\n.form-control--sm keeps 16px type. Below it, Safari on iOS zooms the page in on\nfocus and never zooms back out.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b37b70b2a93c6ed9028d672b24cd3c498e72d112","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/git/trees/b37b70b2a93c6ed9028d672b24cd3c498e72d112"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/git/commits/e9c26181bf99ff92f2114baba128e8147ba6722b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commit/e9c26181bf99ff92f2114baba128e8147ba6722b","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zk4toAKGU5YzI2MTgxYmY5OWZmOTJmMjExNGJhYmExMjhlODE0N2JhNjcyMmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commit/f83a2d7db7f2f1c04b408b6e06e6a3692d9cbc64","sha":"f83a2d7db7f2f1c04b408b6e06e6a3692d9cbc64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commits/f83a2d7db7f2f1c04b408b6e06e6a3692d9cbc64"}],"sha":"e9c26181bf99ff92f2114baba128e8147ba6722b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commits/e9c26181bf99ff92f2114baba128e8147ba6722b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/commits/f83a2d7db7f2f1c04b408b6e06e6a3692d9cbc64/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T11:19:09Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T11:19:09Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"Phase 3G — ApprovalFilter takes an assignee Uid, plus unassignedOnly\n\nThe numeric id only ever worked for the caller''s own, which is why the queue\nfilter could say \"me\" and nothing else. The server resolves the Uid against\njp_sso — the cross-database join in the API layer.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2477f8c5b43210bf1551f63b34b0ca9113edbb4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-shared/git/trees/2477f8c5b43210bf1551f63b34b0ca9113edbb4e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/re