hub.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/91eb3e618722c231c298a36b8acee81e64adf2e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T15:01:24Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T15:01:24Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"6A-0: the approval engine, driven somewhere other than level 1\n\napproval-levels.mjs is 31 assertions against G14''s four questions, and it\nfound the answer to a fifth nobody had asked: an organisation override that\ndid not override. The engine fix is in jp-backend; this is the suite that\nforced it out and the record of what it proved.\n\nTwo of my own tests were wrong first, and both are worth the words.\n\nThe trail assertion did not know the trail opens with the SUBMISSION. Action\ntypes are 1 Approve, 2 Reject, 3 RequestResubmit, 4 Submit, 5 Resubmit, and\nUSP_SubmitApprovalRequest writes its own action-4 row — correctly, because \"who\nasked for this\" is part of the trail. The expectation now names the whole\nsequence, because a trail with a step missing is the failure it is written to\ncatch.\n\nThe organisation-override test asked its question at the wrong level. A\nprevious assertion had already advanced the request to level 2, so the override\nquestion landed there and got a perfectly correct \"approved\" back. It passed\nnothing and proved nothing, which is worse than failing — it is a green line\nthat means a different thing than it says. It has its own fresh request now.\n\nAnd the fixture went from two roles to three. With two, the organisation''s\nlevel-2 role happened to BE the platform default''s level-1 role, which made two\ndistinct properties — \"the check reads this level\" and \"an override replaces\nthe default\" — indistinguishable. Either assertion passing could have meant\neither thing. The third role belongs to neither of the organisation''s levels,\nso refusing it can only be the override.\n\n⚠️ G31 opened rather than fixed. The engine writes an error-log row for every\nordinary concurrency conflict: THROW 50023 lands in the CATCH, and the CATCH\nlogs before translating. That is the opposite of the line 5A drew for\nUSP_ApplyToJob, where the EXPECTED duplicate is swallowed and only an\nunexpected 2601 is logged — two engines, two answers, one question. Changing\nwhat the approval engine logs is an operations decision, not a debt owed to\nG14, and 6A-0''s boundary is G14. So the suite asserts exactly one row, names\nit, and says why.\n\nG14 CLOSED. Three-or-more levels stays untested and says so: 6A seeds one\nlevel, the engine is now proven on two, and writing tests for a depth no\nconsumer asks for is the same assumption G14 was written against.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6e37e58957e9b305a67e3775db0a162fb957acc7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/trees/6e37e58957e9b305a67e3775db0a162fb957acc7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/commits/91eb3e618722c231c298a36b8acee81e64adf2e3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/91eb3e618722c231c298a36b8acee81e64adf2e3","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zoeNoAKDkxZWIzZTYxODcyMmMyMzFjMjk4YTM2YjhhY2VlODFlNjRhZGYyZTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/2762b601acbe898d35732d92231d49a931043467","sha":"2762b601acbe898d35732d92231d49a931043467","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/2762b601acbe898d35732d92231d49a931043467"}],"sha":"91eb3e618722c231c298a36b8acee81e64adf2e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/91eb3e618722c231c298a36b8acee81e64adf2e3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/2762b601acbe898d35732d92231d49a931043467/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T14:42:46Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T14:42:46Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"The race test proved an outcome, not a race — now it proves both\n\nEvery assertion in that section was about the OUTCOME: one row, one inserter,\none ALREADY_APPLIED. All three are equally satisfied by two applies that ran\nseconds apart. If a session connected late and its WAITFOR TIME had already\npassed, it would return immediately, the pair would run sequentially, and the\nsuite would have gone green while testing the plain double-tap path that the\n\"sequential repeat\" check below it already covers. An armed race that silently\ndisarms is exactly the shape of a test that passes for the wrong reason — the\nthing this project has caught three times already and written a rule about.\n\nSo each session now stamps SYSUTCDATETIME() the instant its WAITFOR RETURNS,\nbefore entering the procedure, and again after it returns:\n\n  A  spid 51  2026-09-19T14:39:02.0192818   ran 27 ms, LCK waits 11 ms\n  B  spid 53  2026-09-19T14:39:02.0192818   ran 19 ms, LCK waits 11 ms\n  entry gap 0 ms  ·  execution windows overlap 19 ms\n\nIdentical to the 100-nanosecond digit, on two different spids, with overlapping\nexecution windows — repeated across three runs. The tolerance is 50 ms and it\nwas measured rather than guessed: ten armed runs all released in the same\nmillisecond, the floor being the ~16 ms Windows timer tick that quantises both\nreadings, and any genuine stagger is hundreds of milliseconds at minimum.\n\nLock waits are reported, not asserted. The loser usually blocks on the winner''s\nkey lock — 11 to 28 ms observed — but this transaction is short enough that the\nwinner sometimes commits before the loser ever waits, and one run showed the\nwinner at 0 ms. Asserting it would make the suite flaky for a reason unrelated\nto correctness, so it prints as supporting evidence of real contention.\n\nSection 1B is the part that matters most. The same pair runs again, deliberately\nstaggered by 3 s, through the SAME ranTogether() function — and that function\nmust reject it. It does, at a measured 3000 ms. The staggered pair''s OUTCOME is\nidentical to the race''s: one row, one inserter, one ALREADY_APPLIED. That is\nthe whole argument for capturing the gate instants, demonstrated rather than\nasserted: by outcome alone the two are indistinguishable.\n\nTwo things I got wrong on the way. The stagger asked for 2.5 s and measured\n1997 ms, because WAITFOR TIME takes whole seconds and truncating two sub-second\nbases lands them on adjacent seconds; the base is rounded to a whole second now,\nand the gap is exactly what the comment claims. And the control''s second\napplication broke the 3C negative three sections later — Msg 1505, because that\ntest creates a temporary unique index on TeacherId alone and a teacher holding\ntwo rows makes it impossible to create. Fifth time a fixture has outlived the\nassertion it was made for. It cleans up where it is made.\n\n21/21 -> 28/28. applications-consent 31/31 and applications-lifecycle 75/75\nunchanged; the database is back to zero applications, zero jobs, no temporary\nindex.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9cbada432e1aecc507dbd5be5a1adb6d69440e46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/trees/9cbada432e1aecc507dbd5be5a1adb6d69440e46"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/commits/2762b601acbe898d35732d92231d49a931043467","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/2762b601acbe898d35732d92231d49a931043467","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zoeNoAKDI3NjJiNjAxYWNiZTg5OGQzNTczMmQ5MjIzMWQ0OWE5MzEwNDM0Njc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/f71b929f0b9dd90fbfe0fd6d5885a48fce62a877","sha":"f71b929f0b9dd90fbfe0fd6d5885a48fce62a877","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/f71b929f0b9dd90fbfe0fd6d5885a48fce62a877"}],"sha":"2762b601acbe898d35732d92231d49a931043467","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/2762b601acbe898d35732d92231d49a931043467"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/f71b929f0b9dd90fbfe0fd6d5885a48fce62a877/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T14:29:20Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T14:29:20Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"5B: decision 2.71, three guards deliberately reversed, and one that never ran\n\napplications-screens.mjs is 86 assertions across two apps in a real browser,\nand the negatives are most of it. Every screen-level claim about something\nbeing absent is paired with the request a person could make anyway — from\ndevtools, from curl, from a stale tab — and the SERVER''s answer is what is\nasserted. A suite that only checked rendering would pass just as happily\nagainst a product that drew nothing and enforced nothing.\n\n🔒 The consent boundary is proved from both ends. The teacher applies by\nCLICKING, and the school''s list carries no contact at all — checked against the\nraw bytes, not against null, because every applicant on that list has consented\nand an email there would break the SHAPE rather than the rule. The detail\nunlocks it for the applied-to school; a second school gets zero rows and a 404,\nnever a 403, because \"you may not see THAT one\" confirms it exists.\n\n🔴 The snapshot is shown, not claimed: apply, replace the resume, and the two\nfetches come back with different bytes and different markers, printed.\n\n🔴 The dropdown''s options are matched against the actual masters response\ncaptured off the wire — not against a list this file knows — and the offer\nchain must not appear, while the table still holds all ten because ids are a\ncontract.\n\n⚠️ THREE SUITES HAD THEIR ASSERTIONS REVERSED, and each says why in place.\ndashboards-3i asserted SCHOOL_APPLICANTS was hidden; jobs-screens asserted the\napplicants area still promised a coming release; screens-3i asserted two\ndisabled actions and a 404 at /applicants. All three were correct for 3I and 4B\nand all three describe state 5B changed. Those guards were working; they must\nnot be read as having broken.\n\nNone of the replacements is weaker. screens-3i now reads its expectation FROM\nTHE DATABASE — as many empty states as there are empty tables — which is the\nonly version that keeps meaning what 3I meant: no number without a row behind\nit. jobs-screens requires the promise-copy to be gone and no disabled\nplaceholder to survive. dashboards-3i requires the menu row AND the mockup''s\ndeletion together, because either alone proves nothing.\n\n⚠️ And one guard turned out never to have run. screens-3h looked for\n`#section-experience .empty`; the markup has said `.card-empty` since the 3H\ncommit that introduced both, so the locator matched nothing, textContent() hung\nand the suite died on a timeout before its last three checks. `git show`\nconfirms it is not a 5B regression — that assertion has never once executed. A\nsuite that cannot finish is not one that passes; it is one nobody reads the\noutput of. Fixed, 21/21.\n\n⚠️ FOURTH fixture contamination, and this one was mine. The suite uploaded a\nresume to prove RESUME_REQUIRED and left it there, permanently changing a\nseeded account that local-accounts.md documents as \"a name and a state, 0%\".\nThe next run failed correctly, because the premise it asserts had stopped being\ntrue. The first fix was also wrong: it snapshotted BEFORE normalising, so the\n\"restore\" put the contamination back. It snapshots after, and restores in a\nfinally. Count so far: the 2.5 period rows, the 4B ledger owner, 5A''s\nunverified teacher, now this.\n\nPROJECT_MEMORY: 2.71, progress row, header, close-out — and G29 (the applicants\nlist''s search and paging are client-side over a 200-row cap, with the cap said\nout loud on screen) and G30 (actionLink, closed). G27 is annotated rather than\nclosed: 5B added zero new copies of `.tabs` and deliberately did not promote it,\nbecause the three existing copies differ and a global would leak into screens\nthat omit those properties on purpose.\n\nHOW_TO_RUN''s status header was two phases stale and now says Phase 5 complete,\nwith a teacher walkthrough that names the three things worth trying\ndeliberately. design-screens gains thirteen pictures; the mockup''s two stay as\nhistory, labelled, next to the real screen they became.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9fcd4373c6d763cbbb0502834fcb8993c9d2a12c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/trees/9fcd4373c6d763cbbb0502834fcb8993c9d2a12c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/commits/f71b929f0b9dd90fbfe0fd6d5885a48fce62a877","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/f71b929f0b9dd90fbfe0fd6d5885a48fce62a877","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zoeNoAKGY3MWI5MjlmMGI5ZGQ5MGZiZmUwZmQ2ZDU4ODVhNDhmY2U2MmE4Nzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/cfd9ecacd5085b20bb7bbe92d331a2d0f419d096","sha":"cfd9ecacd5085b20bb7bbe92d331a2d0f419d096","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/cfd9ecacd5085b20bb7bbe92d331a2d0f419d096"}],"sha":"f71b929f0b9dd90fbfe0fd6d5885a48fce62a877","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/f71b929f0b9dd90fbfe0fd6d5885a48fce62a877"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/cfd9ecacd5085b20bb7bbe92d331a2d0f419d096/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T12:32:30Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T12:32:30Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"Phase 5A: decision 2.70, G28, and three suites — the consent boundary and\nthe race are the phase\n\napplications-consent 31/31, applications-race 21/21,\napplications-lifecycle 75/75, swagger floor 76 -> 89.\n\nThe consent suite asserts contact is ABSENT FROM THE BYTES before any\napplication exists — not merely null, not merely hidden. A serialiser or\na mapper can add a key that happens to be undefined, and a CSS rule can\nhide a value that was still sent; neither is the property 2.56 needs. The\nteacher applies, the same call returns contact, and a second school with\nits own active job still gets nothing.\n\nThe race suite runs two genuinely parallel applies armed on one\nwall-clock instant, then does the part that matters: it creates a\nTEMPORARY second unique index, forces a 2601 that is NOT the duplicate\napply, and proves the procedure does not claim ALREADY_APPLIED — it\nsurfaces as itself, names the other index, writes no row, and is logged\nbefore being re-thrown. Then the index is dropped and the SAME call\nsucceeds, which is what makes the whole thing non-vacuous: without that\nstep, \"it was refused\" would have been satisfied by any refusal at all.\n\n🔴 Added an assertion nothing had: an UNVERIFIED teacher can apply. The\nprocedure has no IsVerified clause, which is correct and is exactly the\nkind of correctness a future \"surely we should check this\" edit removes\nwithout anybody noticing. The premise is asserted first — the fixture\nteacher is confirmed unverified in the database — so a drifted fixture\nfails the premise rather than passing the claim for the wrong reason. It\nalso asserts their consent unlocks contact identically, because\nverification never gated that either.\n\n⚠️ That addition then broke an assertion 250 lines downstream: the\nteacher''s own stats read 2 applications instead of 1, because the\nunverified teacher this section picks can be the same teacher that one\nuses. Fixed by cleaning the fixture up immediately, not by loosening the\ncount. Third time in this project a fixture has contaminated a later\ncount — the 2.5 boundary rows, the 4B ledger owner, now this.\n\n2.70 carries the build notes. G28 records the withdraw deferral with its\ntrigger: a teacher cannot withdraw an application in this phase, and a\nhalf-built withdraw that soft-deleted the row would revoke contact\nthrough a path nobody designed.\n\nVerified independently, not taken on report. Every suite above plus\njobs-consume 23/23, jobs-lifecycle 34/34, jobs-screens 55/55, entitlement\n34/34 + 34/34, dashboards 27/27, team 49/49, profile-branches 37/37,\nbackend 0/0, five frontends zero warnings, run_all idempotent.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"23fa92c8558df75417246421b98907780f273f1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/trees/23fa92c8558df75417246421b98907780f273f1a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/commits/cfd9ecacd5085b20bb7bbe92d331a2d0f419d096","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/cfd9ecacd5085b20bb7bbe92d331a2d0f419d096","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zoeNoAKGNmZDllY2FjZDUwODViMjBiYjdiYmU5MmQzMzFhMmQwZjQxOWQwOTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/601c2005c88f1a88cb85e3d65f4a7428b88ed821","sha":"601c2005c88f1a88cb85e3d65f4a7428b88ed821","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/601c2005c88f1a88cb85e3d65f4a7428b88ed821"}],"sha":"cfd9ecacd5085b20bb7bbe92d331a2d0f419d096","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/cfd9ecacd5085b20bb7bbe92d331a2d0f419d096"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/601c2005c88f1a88cb85e3d65f4a7428b88ed821/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T09:26:45Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T09:26:45Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"PRE-5b: the calendar bomb is defused, and PROJECT_MEMORY stops lying\nabout it\n\n🔴 The correction that matters most here is to the memory file, not the\ncode. PRE-5 fixed the bomb in the same session it was found, and I did\nnot update the close-out — so PROJECT_MEMORY went on saying 33/34 with a\n\"suggested fix\" for something already fixed, and the next brief was\nwritten from that stale text. The whole point of that file is to be the\nthing you can trust without re-deriving it, and it failed at exactly that.\n\nThe fix itself was already in (5303da8): section 6''s two boundary rows got\ntheir own OwnerUid and the assertion went from `augUsed >= 1 && sepUsed\n=== 1` to `=== 1` on BOTH sides — stronger than what shipped, because\n`>= 1` was precisely what had been swallowing the contamination.\n\nProven defused rather than dodged: the same two rows read from seven\nvantage points — mid-August, the boundary day either side of 18:30Z,\nSeptember, October, and February 2027 — answer 1 and 1 every time. The\ncounts are blind to what month it is, which is the property that was\nmissing. And the two window-math assertions the test exists for still\nhold: 18:29:59Z lands in August, 18:30:00Z in September.\n\nBaseline is now warning-free: the unused UiButtonComponent import is gone\n(mine, from 4B) and the SCSS budget is re-thresholded in jp-admin with\nits reasoning written down. All five frontends build with zero warnings,\nbackend 0/0.\n\n⚠️ G27 opened: `.tabs` and `.banner` hand-rolled in three components each,\nneither in the design system (2.23). Found while measuring the budget, and\ndeliberately NOT conflated with it — raising a threshold would have hidden\nit, and extracting the patterns would not have cleared the threshold.\n\n34/34. Every other suite unchanged: swagger 10/10, jobs-consume 23/23,\njobs-lifecycle 34/34, entitlement-http 34/34, dashboards 27/27, team\n49/49, profile-branches 37/37.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6db40adb2fcf4b33f5adfccf3ea03fbecf0c15da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/trees/6db40adb2fcf4b33f5adfccf3ea03fbecf0c15da"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/commits/601c2005c88f1a88cb85e3d65f4a7428b88ed821","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/601c2005c88f1a88cb85e3d65f4a7428b88ed821","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zoeNoAKDYwMWMyMDA1Yzg4ZjFhODhjYjg1ZTNkNjVmNGE3NDI4Yjg4ZWQ4MjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/5303da8c4b315144437d33e3b781643cef93c726","sha":"5303da8c4b315144437d33e3b781643cef93c726","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/5303da8c4b315144437d33e3b781643cef93c726"}],"sha":"601c2005c88f1a88cb85e3d65f4a7428b88ed821","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/601c2005c88f1a88cb85e3d65f4a7428b88ed821"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/5303da8c4b315144437d33e3b781643cef93c726/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T09:14:46Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T09:14:46Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"PRE-5: G26 opened and closed, decisions 2.68 and 2.69, a real Viewer\naccount, and a calendar bomb defused\n\nG26 — jp_app masters unreachable through /api/masters/* — opened and\nclosed the same day, because the thing was found and written down in 4B\nand then appeared on no checklist. A consequence recorded in a code\ncomment is not tracked; a gap number is.\n\n2.68 is a rule, not a record, which is why it is its own number rather\nthan a note under 2.66: it applies to every future master and will be\ncited. Same shape as 2.61, where the incident stayed in G25 and the rule\ngot a number. It states in both directions that these are true masters\nwith normal caching, and that the gating prohibition belongs only to\nm_mdm_features and m_mdm_plan_features.\n\n2.69 retires the Viewer fixture. jobs-screens used to soft-delete the HR\nrole''s JOB.CREATE and JOB.EDIT grants, assert read-only rendering, and put\nthem back — honest, asserted at both ends, and still editing a SHARED ROLE\nto test a screen, so a killed run left the real HR account weakened until\nsomebody noticed. viewer@greenwood.edu.in is now seeded through the\nproduct''s own invite flow (scripts/seed-school-viewer.mjs), and the suite\nno longer writes to t_sso_role_permissions in either direction.\n\n⚠️ The old fixture also passed for the wrong reason: HR is in another\nschool, so \"no New job button\" was true of an EMPTY list. The seeded\nViewer sits in the owner''s school and sees three rows, so read-only is\nnow distinguished from empty — which is what the assertion was supposed\nto be about.\n\n🔴 Fixed a calendar bomb in entitlement-engine that I wrote in 2.5. Its\nperiod-boundary fixture shared an owner with the sections above it, and\nthose consume through USP_ConsumeFeature, which stamps OccurredOn =\nSYSUTCDATETIME(). Written in August the four earlier consumes fell into\nAugust, where `augUsed >= 1` swallowed them; in September they moved\nacross and sepUsed read 5 instead of 1. Green for a month, then\ndeterministically red, with nothing about the engine having changed.\n\nFixed by isolating the fixture to its own owner, not by loosening the\nassertion — `sepUsed === 1` is the part that proves the 18:30:00Z row\ncrossed the boundary, and `>= 1` would have made it unable to fail for\nthe right reason. It is now `=== 1` on BOTH sides, which is stronger than\nwhat shipped.\n\njobs-screens 37/37 -> 55/55. The new assertions capture the masters\nresponse OFF THE WIRE and match every rendered option against it — a\nhardcoded array renders identically, so counting options would prove\nnothing. A Part-time job then round-trips through the database row and\nthe API JSON, with the 2.61 dual read asserting the row is 1 FIRST and\nthe JSON true second.\n\nAlso asserts USP_GetMaster and USP_GetAppMaster claim disjoint key sets,\nread out of sys.sql_modules. Nothing in either database can enforce that,\nand an overlap would be answered by jp_mdm silently for ever.\n\nAll verified independently, not taken on report: swagger 10/10,\njobs-consume 23/23, jobs-lifecycle 34/34, entitlement-engine 34/34,\nentitlement-http 34/34, dashboards 27/27, team 49/49, profile-branches\n37/37, jobs-screens 55/55, backend 0/0, five frontends built, run_all\ntwice with identical object counts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f654aad4ca09b546e6a631ef7f24ea6d503a9686","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/trees/f654aad4ca09b546e6a631ef7f24ea6d503a9686"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/commits/5303da8c4b315144437d33e3b781643cef93c726","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/5303da8c4b315144437d33e3b781643cef93c726","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zoeNoAKDUzMDNkYThjNGIzMTUxNDQ0MzdkMzNlM2I3ODE2NDNjZWY5M2M3MjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/ce11b205db8878010a35ceb06807e4d13954b38a","sha":"ce11b205db8878010a35ceb06807e4d13954b38a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/ce11b205db8878010a35ceb06807e4d13954b38a"}],"sha":"5303da8c4b315144437d33e3b781643cef93c726","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/5303da8c4b315144437d33e3b781643cef93c726"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/ce11b205db8878010a35ceb06807e4d13954b38a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T12:58:17Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T12:58:17Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"Swagger guard, and decision 2.67\n\nverify:swagger — both APIs'' documents return 200, parse as OpenAPI, carry\nunique schema ids, and have not shrunk below a recorded floor.\n\n🔴 The floor is the part that matters. A 500 is loud and would be noticed\neventually. A controller that quietly stops being discovered — a routing\nmistake, an accidental [ApiExplorerSettings], a class that stops being\npublic — still returns 200 and still parses. The document is simply\nsmaller, and nothing else in the build would notice. Floors: SSO 21,\nApp 76.\n\n⚠️ A floor, not an equality: adding endpoints is normal and must not fail\nthis. Removing them deliberately means lowering the number in the same\ncommit, with a reason.\n\nThe two endpoints most likely to be missed are also asserted by name, so\nthe count staying level while one vanished and another appeared cannot\npass.\n\n🔴 The guard was watched failing before being trusted: the floor was\nraised to 999, it failed with \"76 found, floor 999\", and was set back. A\nguard nobody has seen fail is a guard nobody knows works.\n\n⚠️ It is NOT in run_all.sql, and cannot be — that is a sqlcmd script and\ncannot make an HTTP call. It lives with the other verification scripts\nand in package.json.\n\n2.67 records why this survived so long: every suite was green throughout\nbecause none of them fetches swagger.json. They call the endpoints\ndirectly, which work perfectly well without a document. The API was\nbroken in a way the tests were shaped not to look at — the same lesson as\n3I, one layer over.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7fdba48b3d94f82cb564ba143f1631d37f788b7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/trees/7fdba48b3d94f82cb564ba143f1631d37f788b7d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/commits/ce11b205db8878010a35ceb06807e4d13954b38a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/ce11b205db8878010a35ceb06807e4d13954b38a","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zoeNoAKGNlMTFiMjA1ZGI4ODc4MDEwYTM1Y2ViMDY4MDdlNGQxMzk1NGIzOGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/0cb615f927a865981dc8d2f9d3df377e4a2edfbb","sha":"0cb615f927a865981dc8d2f9d3df377e4a2edfbb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/0cb615f927a865981dc8d2f9d3df377e4a2edfbb"}],"sha":"ce11b205db8878010a35ceb06807e4d13954b38a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/ce11b205db8878010a35ceb06807e4d13954b38a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/0cb615f927a865981dc8d2f9d3df377e4a2edfbb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T12:31:03Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T12:31:03Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"Phase 4B: decision 2.66, jobs-screens 37/37, Phase 4 closed\n\n2.65''s pending list is done and the phase is ✅. jobs-screens.mjs 37/37;\nevery earlier suite unchanged.\n\nThe chain 2.5 and 2.64 each proved half of is now proven whole, in one\nbrowser session across BOTH apps with no restart between the flip and the\nattempt: JOB_POST set to METERED on the admin screen (a select change,\nnot SQL), then in jp-school the first publish consumes, the second is\nrefused with the quota message and the job stays a Draft, then back to\nFREE on the admin screen and the same job publishes with the ledger\nunchanged.\n\nTwo script bugs found by running it, both fixed and both noted where they\nwere:\n\n  orgUid resolved the lowest BranchId across ALL schools — a different\n  school entirely — so every ledger assertion counted an organisation\n  nobody was acting as, read 0, and reported the engine as broken. A\n  fixture pointing at the wrong row does not fail loudly; it fails as a\n  wrong number.\n\n  The ledger was cleared on exit but not on entry, so the previous\n  (wrong-org) run''s teardown deleted a different organisation''s rows and\n  left a real one behind. Cleaning up on exit is not enough when the exit\n  path can itself be wrong. Both ends now, with the starting value\n  asserted rather than assumed.\n\nThe verification also surfaced a real UI defect by printing the toast\ntext: one refusal, two messages. Fixed in jp-shared.\n\n⚠️ The \"Viewer\" is synthesised and says so: no SCHOOL_VIEWER account is\nseeded, and the UI decides from permissions rather than roles, so HR''s\ngrants are reduced to JOB.VIEW and restored — asserted at both ends.\n\n🔴 Two endpoint gaps were reported rather than quietly filled. One was\napproved and added (GET /api/jobs/stats). The other is left open:\nemployment types have no master endpoint, and the five values were NOT\nhardcoded because 2.7 forbids exactly that. The consequence is written\ndown — a school cannot currently post a Part-time or Contract vacancy.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d2e3f74747a11af0c8a5b0d41bb064a83a56e0c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/trees/d2e3f74747a11af0c8a5b0d41bb064a83a56e0c9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/commits/0cb615f927a865981dc8d2f9d3df377e4a2edfbb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/0cb615f927a865981dc8d2f9d3df377e4a2edfbb","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zoeNoAKDBjYjYxNWY5MjdhODY1OTgxZGM4ZDJmOWQzZGYzNzdlNGEyZWRmYmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/ade011a48d5f9200d82c8aae09db61a3cdcefd0e","sha":"ade011a48d5f9200d82c8aae09db61a3cdcefd0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/ade011a48d5f9200d82c8aae09db61a3cdcefd0e"}],"sha":"0cb615f927a865981dc8d2f9d3df377e4a2edfbb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/0cb615f927a865981dc8d2f9d3df377e4a2edfbb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/ade011a48d5f9200d82c8aae09db61a3cdcefd0e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T11:19:03Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T11:19:03Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"Phase 4 backend: decision 2.65, two verification suites, and the\nmaster-data warning for demos\n\njobs-consume 23/23 and jobs-lifecycle 34/34, both fresh, both asserting\nthe shipped state on entry AND restoring it on exit.\n\njobs-consume proves the engine wiring: JOB_POST flipped to METERED\nquota 1 through the admin API, first publish consumes and the ledger row\ncarries the JOB''S OWN Uid, second publish is refused with the job still a\nDraft and no row written, restored to FREE and publishing consumes\nnothing. Then the atomicity negative — a temporary AFTER UPDATE trigger\nfires between the consume and the commit, and both the job status and the\nledger roll back together. Then the republish: close, publish again,\nALREADY_CONSUMED with the original entry id and still one row.\n\n⚠️ The atomicity test is only worth something because of the step after\nit: with the injection removed, the SAME publish succeeds and DOES\nconsume. Without that, \"job stayed a Draft, ledger stayed empty\" is\nsatisfied by any failure at all — which is precisely how the first\nversion of this test passed while proving nothing.\n\njobs-lifecycle covers the rest: the full draft-edit-publish-list-close\npath with JSON at each step, the 2.61 dual read, the structural lock\nrefusing a subject swap while terms still edit, the cross-tenant scope\nnegatives on CREATE and EDIT (both NOT_FOUND, never FORBIDDEN, and no\nresponse leaking SchoolId), HR refused publish and close because the seed\nwithholds them, expiry derived with the stored row and the API response\nprinted side by side, and five validation refusals each with its own\ncode.\n\nHOW_TO_RUN gains a warning aimed at the job form: every dropdown on it —\nsubject, designation, qualification, class level — is still our\nguess-seed, five of them marked PROVISIONAL. Say so once during a demo,\nor the question arrives afterwards.\n\n⚠️ PROJECT_MEMORY records the phase as BACKEND COMPLETE, SCREENS PENDING,\nand 2.65 lists exactly what is left. Nothing is half-built: the backend\nstands complete with its verification, and no screen was started.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8ecb09515279eeadd75b35098e19e4f2d84b71bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/trees/8ecb09515279eeadd75b35098e19e4f2d84b71bd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/commits/ade011a48d5f9200d82c8aae09db61a3cdcefd0e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/ade011a48d5f9200d82c8aae09db61a3cdcefd0e","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zoeNoAKGFkZTAxMWE0OGQ1ZjkyMDBkODJjOGFhZTA5ZGI2MWEzY2RjZWZkMGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/363f4b3589e8c5462b474bc5a3daed044a71dc60","sha":"363f4b3589e8c5462b474bc5a3daed044a71dc60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/363f4b3589e8c5462b474bc5a3daed044a71dc60"}],"sha":"ade011a48d5f9200d82c8aae09db61a3cdcefd0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/ade011a48d5f9200d82c8aae09db61a3cdcefd0e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/363f4b3589e8c5462b474bc5a3daed044a71dc60/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T10:19:41Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T10:19:41Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"Verification: name the last-unit boundary, and restore to the shipped\nstate rather than to whatever was found\n\nThe three calls were already asserted individually. What makes them a\nboundary is running back to back on one owner without the fixture being\ntouched between them:\n\n  1. spend the last unit       -> Status 1, quotaRemaining 0\n  2. retry the SAME reference  -> 200, ALREADY_CONSUMED, original entry id\n  3. a FRESH reference         -> 400, QUOTA_EXHAUSTED\n\nStep 2 is the bug this phase fixed. Step 3 is what proves the fix did not\novershoot: the reference check now runs ahead of the quota decision, and\nif it matched too loosely or short-circuited that branch, a fresh\nreference would be allowed and quota would have quietly stopped being\nenforced. The two only mean something together.\n\nAdded the assertions that were missing: the retry returns the ORIGINAL\nentry id and writes nothing, and the ledger holds exactly one live\nconsume across all three calls.\n\nAlso fixed a real flaw in the script''s teardown. It captured JOB_POST''s\nmode on the way in and put that value back on the way out, which is wrong\nin the one situation that actually occurs: if a previous run dies before\nits teardown -- killed, timed out, or a truncated pipe closing stdout --\nthe next run reads the dirty state as \"original\" and faithfully preserves\nit. Two runs later nobody knows the real baseline.\n\nIt now restores to the documented shipped state (every feature FREE and\nactive, no plan mappings), which the script already asserts as its\npremise, and resets to that on the way IN as well so it is self-healing\nafter a kill.\n\nFound by killing it: a Select-Object -First in the shell terminated the\npipeline mid-run, the teardown never ran, and the next run failed its own\npremise check -- which is the assertion doing its job.\n\nentitlement-http 34/34, entitlement-engine 34/34, run back to back, with\nthe database ending in the shipped state both times.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"43b0c1dc29c3aee6eada5264525cc7a033718771","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/trees/43b0c1dc29c3aee6eada5264525cc7a033718771"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/commits/363f4b3589e8c5462b474bc5a3daed044a71dc60","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/363f4b3589e8c5462b474bc5a3daed044a71dc60","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zoeNoAKDM2M2Y0YjM1ODllOGM1NDYyYjQ3NGJjNWEzZGFlZDA0NGE3MWRjNjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/8962a36fa341579d052c2f2ffddff0ebf16f6f39","sha":"8962a36fa341579d052c2f2ffddff0ebf16f6f39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/8962a36fa341579d052c2f2ffddff0ebf16f6f39"}],"sha":"363f4b3589e8c5462b474bc5a3daed044a71dc60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/363f4b3589e8c5462b474bc5a3daed044a71dc60"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/8962a36fa341579d052c2f2ffddff0ebf16f6f39/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T10:04:08Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T10:04:08Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"Phase 2.5: decision 2.64, three verification suites, and the design doc\ncorrected where the build disagreed with it\n\nThe engine is built and gated on nothing. PROJECT_MEMORY carries the\nbuild notes; MONETIZATION_DESIGN.md carries three corrections marked in\nplace rather than silently edited.\n\nCorrections to the design:\n\n  Reversals are no longer summed into a balance. The original formula\n  listed \"Reversal +N\", which double-counts -- and for a reversed QUOTA\n  consume it invented a credit outright, because that consume was never\n  part of the credit balance. Every refunded job post would have handed\n  the school a free one.\n\n  The reference is checked before the quota decision. The index alone\n  only produces ALREADY_CONSUMED when the request would otherwise have\n  been allowed, so a retry of an already-paid action was refused with\n  QUOTA_EXHAUSTED once quota ran out.\n\n  A consume never splits across quota and credits. Forced by the\n  idempotency index, and stated by neither decision on its own.\n\nThree suites, all fresh:\n\n  entitlement-engine.mjs 34/34 -- the race runs two sqlcmd sessions armed\n  for the same wall-clock instant, the 2C pattern; one consumes, the\n  other gets QUOTA_EXHAUSTED, and the ledger holds exactly one row. Also\n  the quota-before-credits order, the reversal path, every refusal code\n  from a real call including SUBSCRIPTION_MISSING via a deliberately\n  broken row, and the IST period boundary at 18:29:59Z versus 18:30:00Z\n  on 31 August.\n\n  entitlement-http.mjs 31/31 -- the 2.61 dual read on the one column\n  where a silent false would refuse everything everywhere, every refusal\n  code as a distinct HTTP status, ALREADY_CONSUMED as a 200 carrying a\n  code, the kill switch live, and both isolation greps with their output\n  shown.\n\n  screens-25.mjs 19/19 -- the flip through the admin screen with nothing\n  between the click and the consume.\n\nTwo test premises were wrong before they were right, and both are noted\nwhere they were fixed: QUOTA_EXHAUSTED was asserted against a fixture\nthat still held credits, and the \"unmapped is never blank\" check ran\nagainst a screen with zero unmapped cells and passed while proving\nnothing. An assertion that cannot fail is worse than none, because it is\ncounted.\n\nHOW_TO_RUN gains a section saying the engine is built and inert, and\nwarning against presenting the Plans screen as a price list -- pricing has\nnot been agreed and m_mdm_plans still holds two free plans.\n\nQ4''s frontend-split cell now carries the ~4 dev-day planning estimate,\nlabelled as an estimate rather than a measurement. The unacknowledged\nscope total is ~16 dev-days across two additions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"60c390187f469275655121c3c7f7bfd74e18551d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/trees/60c390187f469275655121c3c7f7bfd74e18551d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/commits/8962a36fa341579d052c2f2ffddff0ebf16f6f39","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/8962a36fa341579d052c2f2ffddff0ebf16f6f39","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zoeNoAKDg5NjJhMzZmYTM0MTU3OWQwNTJjMmYyZmZkZGZmMGViZjE2ZjZmMzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/c176fc597fc34ba020787bb4e29401c1c2f0bc26","sha":"c176fc597fc34ba020787bb4e29401c1c2f0bc26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/c176fc597fc34ba020787bb4e29401c1c2f0bc26"}],"sha":"8962a36fa341579d052c2f2ffddff0ebf16f6f39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/8962a36fa341579d052c2f2ffddff0ebf16f6f39"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/c176fc597fc34ba020787bb4e29401c1c2f0bc26/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T14:14:15Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T14:14:15Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"2.5-PRE follow-up: gating reads bypass the master cache, and Q4 corrected\n\nThree documentation fixes. No code, no schema, no migrations.\n\n1. MONETIZATION_DESIGN.md gains \"Gating reads never come from the\n   master cache\".\n\n   The mechanism is worth stating precisely, because the danger is not\n   where it first looks. The API holds no server-side cache at all --\n   MasterService reads the database every call, and the hour is a\n   ResponseCache(Location = Client) directive plus Angular''s in-memory\n   cache. So there is no stale-cache bug today. The trap is that\n   features and gating modes ARE master data by every structural test,\n   which makes IMasterService the obvious place to put them, and\n   IMasterService is the obvious place to add an IMemoryCache.\n\n   Chose (a), a direct read per consume. Note what that is: the read is\n   already in the design, because the two databases cannot join. The\n   decision is to write down that it may never become a cache.\n   Affordable because a consume is already a write under a per-owner\n   lock, and consumes are single-digit per school per month rather than\n   masters/bulk on every app load. Admin-flip-to-visible latency is the\n   next consume.\n\n   Rejected (b), short-TTL with invalidation on write. It is correct\n   only while one process owns both the admin screen and the consume\n   path, and under two instances it fails in the worst available shape:\n   the feature is off for some requests and on for others, with no way\n   to tell from outside which is which. (a) needs no such assumption --\n   under multiple instances nothing changes, because there is no second\n   copy to go incoherent.\n\n   An hour of lag would also have made Decision 1 self-refuting: it\n   chose Is_Active over a fourth mode precisely because it restores\n   cleanly during an incident.\n\n   Enforced structurally rather than by comment, per 2.36''s precedent:\n   a dedicated IEntitlementRepository resolving feature and mapping in\n   one query, plus an isolation grep in the phase.\n\n2. The mode-flip test must prove the flip live, not eventually. Assert\n   on the consume path with no restart, no sleep and no cache clear --\n   each of those passes against the broken implementation. Assert the\n   specific Code and both directions; a refusal-only check passes if\n   the feature was already denied for another reason, which is 3G''s\n   vacuous assertion repeating itself.\n\n3. PROJECT_MEMORY:\n   - The header was stale since Phase 0 while the file ran to 3I -- the\n     first line of the first file every session reads. Fixed, and\n     updating it is now part of the close-out checklist. 3I caught this\n     exact class of thing in HOW_TO_RUN and missed it here.\n   - Q4 corrected. The engine is NOT blocked on the client: every\n     feature seeds FREE, so a \"no\" would not change one line. Billing\n     is what waits. Yesterday''s row said otherwise and made Phase 4\n     look like it was waiting on an email.\n   - The risk is named with a number rather than a phrase: roughly 12\n     dev-days of engine work, unbilled and unacknowledged, against a\n     fixed fee -- and it is a list of two, with the frontend split\n     alongside it, because a slip is made by both together and they\n     will be hard to justify separately later. The frontend split''s\n     cell is deliberately empty; it was never estimated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c8b3655147fc6fb45117469f0e6b71ed48b89429","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/trees/c8b3655147fc6fb45117469f0e6b71ed48b89429"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/commits/c176fc597fc34ba020787bb4e29401c1c2f0bc26","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/c176fc597fc34ba020787bb4e29401c1c2f0bc26","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zoeNoAKGMxNzZmYzU5N2ZjMzRiYTAyMDc4N2JiNGUyOTQwMWMxYzJmMGJjMjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/f6ac72337fa3bd066eb96f7e5b6357e3cc8b062e","sha":"f6ac72337fa3bd066eb96f7e5b6357e3cc8b062e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/f6ac72337fa3bd066eb96f7e5b6357e3cc8b062e"}],"sha":"c176fc597fc34ba020787bb4e29401c1c2f0bc26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/c176fc597fc34ba020787bb4e29401c1c2f0bc26"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/f6ac72337fa3bd066eb96f7e5b6357e3cc8b062e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T13:46:50Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T13:46:50Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"Phase 2.5-PRE: write MONETIZATION_DESIGN.md, reconcile scope\n\nThe engine phase stopped because its prompt named a design document that\ndid not exist -- the design was agreed verbally and never written down.\nThis pays that debt. No engine code, no schema scripts, no migrations.\n\nSix decisions, each with the rejected alternative:\n\n- Three gating modes (Free/Boolean/Metered) with Is_Active as the kill\n  switch, not four modes. A mode-based Disabled destroys the mode it\n  replaces, so restoring it depends on somebody remembering.\n- Teacher-search is Boolean, invites are Metered. This is 2.56 expressed\n  as a catalog: searching is looking, inviting is reach, and reach is\n  what is sold.\n- A Boolean check writes nothing to the ledger. A row that can never\n  change a balance is an access log wearing a ledger''s clothes, and it\n  would outnumber the real rows.\n- Credits stay per-feature and non-fungible; the stuck-money case is\n  named where support will meet it, with a human remedy that stays\n  auditable (reversal + grant).\n- Idempotency is a filtered unique index on the action''s reference, and\n  a reversal frees that reference -- a refund must not permanently\n  block redoing the thing that was refunded.\n- Quota periods are calendar months on IST boundaries, derived by\n  counting consumes rather than reset by a scheduler.\n\nTwo directions are argued against in writing rather than quietly\nfollowed (four modes; \"show the ledger rows a reset produces\"). Both\ncarry each position and what adopting the other would cost.\n\nNo conflict with the 2F tables or any locked decision, so no CONFLICTS\nsection. One prerequisite found: jp_app has no IST helper functions\nwhile jp_sso and jp_mdm both do -- the ledger''s periods are IST and\ncross-database calls are forbidden (2.2), so that is Phase 2.5''s first\nscript.\n\nPROJECT_MEMORY reconciliation:\n- Section 3 split \"Subscription & billing\" -- the engine is MVP (2.5),\n  billing is 6.5. As written the line was already false: the\n  subscription table has been shipped since 2F and carries 15 rows.\n- Q4 now records the verbal yes and that the written confirmation the\n  build waits on is still outstanding.\n- Decision 2.63 covers only what is decided here; the six design\n  decisions are referenced, not copied, so the two documents cannot\n  drift apart.\n- Two stale claims fixed in passing: Phase 2.5 still listed payment\n  gateway and invoices, and the milestone paragraph still said the\n  applicants screen runs on fixture data after 3I removed it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"949ebfddc32f38268c23c10978b694357069da90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/trees/949ebfddc32f38268c23c10978b694357069da90"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/commits/f6ac72337fa3bd066eb96f7e5b6357e3cc8b062e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/f6ac72337fa3bd066eb96f7e5b6357e3cc8b062e","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zoeNoAKGY2YWM3MjMzN2ZhM2JkMDY2ZWI5NmY3ZTViNjM1N2UzY2M4YjA2MmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/2bd80341ad2f387f4242c9e367568bcd0d934137","sha":"2bd80341ad2f387f4242c9e367568bcd0d934137","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/2bd80341ad2f387f4242c9e367568bcd0d934137"}],"sha":"f6ac72337fa3bd066eb96f7e5b6357e3cc8b062e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/f6ac72337fa3bd066eb96f7e5b6357e3cc8b062e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/2bd80341ad2f387f4242c9e367568bcd0d934137/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T13:20:33Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T13:20:33Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"Phase 3I — 2.61 locked, G6 closed, and HOW_TO_RUN made true again\n\nDecision 2.61: every procedure returning a standard underscore column to a DTO\nmust alias it, and every phase''s HTTP verification must read BOTH the database\nrow and the JSON for one such field. The failure is silent — the property\ndefaults to false — so nothing else catches it. G25 stays as the incident that\nproduced the rule.\n\nG6 closed. Two of its three bullets had been false since 2D and 2E: the admin\napproval UI existed and JP.App.Api had endpoints. A gap file goes stale too.\n\nHOW_TO_RUN: the header had said \"Phase 1 complete\" since Phase 1. The happy path\ntold people to approve schools through Swagger, which stopped being true in 2E.\nThe \"What is real and what is a mockup\" section is now \"What is real and what is\nnot built yet\", and says plainly that the static-mockup category is empty. Menu\ncounts corrected against the seeded rows rather than assumed — 8, not 9.\n\nProgress log: the two \"⬜ Next\" rows for 2E and 2F screens are gone; both\nshipped months of phases ago.\n\n⚠️ The verification numbers in this phase''s row were placeholders while the work\nwas in progress. They are the real ones now: 27/27 and 16/16.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"17df1ad02f7eb455437acecdf312f07e09e89791","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/trees/17df1ad02f7eb455437acecdf312f07e09e89791"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/commits/2bd80341ad2f387f4242c9e367568bcd0d934137","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/2bd80341ad2f387f4242c9e367568bcd0d934137","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zoeNoAKDJiZDgwMzQxYWQyZjM4N2Y0MjQyYzllMzY3NTY4YmNkMGQ5MzQxMzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/f527da4899aba0408e87fea626b84e29c11dda6e","sha":"f527da4899aba0408e87fea626b84e29c11dda6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/f527da4899aba0408e87fea626b84e29c11dda6e"}],"sha":"2bd80341ad2f387f4242c9e367568bcd0d934137","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/2bd80341ad2f387f4242c9e367568bcd0d934137"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/f527da4899aba0408e87fea626b84e29c11dda6e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T12:41:32Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T12:41:32Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"Phase 3H — decision 2.60, and two verification scripts\n\nteacher-profile.mjs does every mutation to a throwaway account it signs up\nitself, because Rohit, Anita and Imran are worth more intact — they are the only\nhalf-filled profiles in the system and re-seeding them is not a thing anybody\nwants to do twice.\n\n⚠️ The experience arithmetic is asserted EXACTLY. The first version allowed ±1\nand passed, which is useless: a one-month error is precisely the bug 3D found. A\nclosed job counts its final month (Jun 2015 – May 2018 is 36); a current job\ncounts only completed months. Both rules are now written down and checked.\n\nscreens-3h.mjs opens the screen as each of the three and checks what a person\nactually sees — that 0% is never printed as a verdict, that the next step is\nnamed with a reason, and that twenty selections neither inflate the control nor\nscroll the page sideways at 375. It saves nothing: the fixtures stay fixtures,\nverified afterwards.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"28cedb477086128f236ba113592486dd69a5fbef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/trees/28cedb477086128f236ba113592486dd69a5fbef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/commits/f527da4899aba0408e87fea626b84e29c11dda6e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/f527da4899aba0408e87fea626b84e29c11dda6e","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zoeNoAKGY1MjdkYTQ4OTlhYmEwNDA4ZTg3ZmVhNjI2Yjg0ZTI5YzExZGRhNmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/361f4c3a40363ae0e902b5bdd6e7793fe5305233","sha":"361f4c3a40363ae0e902b5bdd6e7793fe5305233","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/361f4c3a40363ae0e902b5bdd6e7793fe5305233"}],"sha":"f527da4899aba0408e87fea626b84e29c11dda6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/f527da4899aba0408e87fea626b84e29c11dda6e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/361f4c3a40363ae0e902b5bdd6e7793fe5305233/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T11:59:41Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T11:59:41Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"Phase 3F — decision 2.59, G25, and two verification scripts\n\nprofile-branches.mjs checks round trips by saving, re-reading and comparing —\nincluding the photo order, which is where the reorder bug hid, and isActive,\nwhich is read from both the column and the JSON.\n\nscreens-3f.mjs drives a real browser for the three claims no HTTP check can\nsettle: the head-office row has no Remove button at all rather than a greyed\none, a single-campus school sees no Campuses entry and gets redirected if it\ntypes the URL, and neither screen scrolls sideways at 375. Screenshots at both\nwidths are in screenshots/3f/.\n\nG25 records the class of bug behind isActive: a standard column with an\nunderscore does not reach its DTO property, nothing fails, and the value simply\narrives as the type''s default.\n\nteam-contract.mjs now removes the campus it creates and waits out the login\nrate limiter instead of failing on it — a script that leaves fixtures behind\nends up verifying its own leftovers, which is how the demo school ended up with\ntwo campuses called North Wing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"af21e3946e629d649d57d16a5076f087d1c741e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/trees/af21e3946e629d649d57d16a5076f087d1c741e6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/commits/361f4c3a40363ae0e902b5bdd6e7793fe5305233","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/361f4c3a40363ae0e902b5bdd6e7793fe5305233","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zoeNoAKDM2MWY0YzNhNDAzNjNhZTBlOTAyYjViZGQ2ZTc3OTNmZTUzMDUyMzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/cad26c2a7a20c94b7079139e281809779b8ed9a2","sha":"cad26c2a7a20c94b7079139e281809779b8ed9a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/cad26c2a7a20c94b7079139e281809779b8ed9a2"}],"sha":"361f4c3a40363ae0e902b5bdd6e7793fe5305233","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/361f4c3a40363ae0e902b5bdd6e7793fe5305233"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/cad26c2a7a20c94b7079139e281809779b8ed9a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T11:19:17Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T11:19:17Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"Phase 3G — decision 2.58, G15 closed, G24 opened\n\nRecords the four owner rules and why they live in the procedures; the\nfull-set sync that must not remove a campus the caller could not see; the\ncross-database invitation and its retry path; and the two things the\nverification corrected — an HTML comment being delivered inside every\ninvitation email, and what \"revoked\" actually does to a stateless JWT.\n\nteam-contract.mjs follows an invitation all the way through: token out of the\nrendered email, password set, sign-in, then removal.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f697e1bdbfe7f1f2800a611a6b389c1ee751fcec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/trees/f697e1bdbfe7f1f2800a611a6b389c1ee751fcec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/commits/cad26c2a7a20c94b7079139e281809779b8ed9a2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/cad26c2a7a20c94b7079139e281809779b8ed9a2","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zoeNoAKGNhZDI2YzJhN2EyMGM5NGI3MDc5MTM5ZTI4MTgwOTc3OWI4ZWQ5YTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/5597c8f82fdf9789bc364df78bd35056b102a79f","sha":"5597c8f82fdf9789bc364df78bd35056b102a79f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/5597c8f82fdf9789bc364df78bd35056b102a79f"}],"sha":"cad26c2a7a20c94b7079139e281809779b8ed9a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/cad26c2a7a20c94b7079139e281809779b8ed9a2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/5597c8f82fdf9789bc364df78bd35056b102a79f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T10:21:52Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T10:21:52Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"PROJECT_MEMORY: Phase 3E — decision 2.57, G23 opened\n\n2.57 records the three layers now protecting contact details, with the proof\nthat the third one works — the browse DTO was deliberately widened, the build\npassed, and the API refused to start naming the property. It also records the\nfull browse field list from a real response body, the 403 message, and the two\nassertions 3C could not write, now closed as real HTTP 404s.\n\nG23: a user can belong to exactly one school as far as the API is concerned.\nNobody has two today, but the shape already exists — Greenwood has two schools\nunder one organisation — and the day a group puts its principal on both, every\nschool screen closes for them. The two ways to fix it are written down along\nwith why the easy one is an IDOR risk, and the decision is deliberately deferred\nuntil a real multi-school group exists rather than guessed at now.\n\nAlso removed an orphaned section left by an earlier splice: the anchor\n''## Uske baad'' matched inside ''### Uske baad screens'', so the replacement cut in\nthe wrong place. Same class of bug as the progress row that once landed on line\n1, and the reason placement is verified after every write.\n\nNext Action is 3F — the screens — with the three seeded half-filled profiles\nnamed as what to build against, and the two API contracts the UI has to honour:\nfull-set sync, and never asking for contact.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"04c7ff98fbaedfd12d8eaec48ff750062a8c9fcc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/trees/04c7ff98fbaedfd12d8eaec48ff750062a8c9fcc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/commits/5597c8f82fdf9789bc364df78bd35056b102a79f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/5597c8f82fdf9789bc364df78bd35056b102a79f","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zoeNoAKDU1OTdjOGY4MmZkZjk3ODliYzM2NGRmNzhiZDM1MDU2YjEwMmE3OWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/c29e3e95dcb2b2ae0e540df0c51821d21aa7cf94","sha":"c29e3e95dcb2b2ae0e540df0c51821d21aa7cf94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/c29e3e95dcb2b2ae0e540df0c51821d21aa7cf94"}],"sha":"5597c8f82fdf9789bc364df78bd35056b102a79f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/5597c8f82fdf9789bc364df78bd35056b102a79f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/c29e3e95dcb2b2ae0e540df0c51821d21aa7cf94/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T00:10:07Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T00:10:07Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"PROJECT_MEMORY: 2.56 LOCKED — contact unlocks on consent, not payment\n\nRecords the resolution of the conflict between 3D''s contact rule and the\nmonetization plan, with the reasoning: what is sold is the school''s capability —\nsearch, invite volume, placement — and never the teacher''s contact details.\n\n2.54 is corrected IN PLACE rather than left standing beside it. It said contact\nunlocks \"only on apply\", and its warning said \"do not widen this to invites\",\nwhich read as excluding accepted invites too. Both are rewritten to point at\n2.56. A half-superseded decision is how somebody reverts this in three months —\nthe same reasoning that removed the npm decision outright in 2.41 instead of\nmarking it superseded.\n\nAlso flagged, because it is the way this gets quietly broken again: the spec\ngives t_app_teacher_invites the statuses Sent / Viewed / Applied / Ignored, and\nnone of them means \"the teacher said yes\". Phase 6 must add ACCEPTED or path 2\ncollapses into path 1 and does nothing.\n\nAdded to the pre-flight checklist with a concrete tripwire: if a plan or\nsubscription is ever named inside fn_TeacherContactUnlocked, the decision has\nbeen broken.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"19ab4bbb2de0574044d43480059a16df5af116f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/trees/19ab4bbb2de0574044d43480059a16df5af116f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/commits/c29e3e95dcb2b2ae0e540df0c51821d21aa7cf94","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/c29e3e95dcb2b2ae0e540df0c51821d21aa7cf94","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zoeNoAKGMyOWUzZTk1ZGNiMmIyYWUwZTU0MGRmMGM1MTgyMWQyMWFhN2NmOTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/2cc3856914a38f103f16a612c923c4717e51e809","sha":"2cc3856914a38f103f16a612c923c4717e51e809","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/2cc3856914a38f103f16a612c923c4717e51e809"}],"sha":"c29e3e95dcb2b2ae0e540df0c51821d21aa7cf94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/c29e3e95dcb2b2ae0e540df0c51821d21aa7cf94"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/2cc3856914a38f103f16a612c923c4717e51e809/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T23:55:23Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T23:55:23Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"PROJECT_MEMORY: Phase 3D — decisions 2.54 and 2.55, G0 closed\n\n2.54 records the teacher-side scope rule and why it is structural rather than a\ncheck, where the contact line is drawn and the three reasons for it, the resume\nbeing a contact detail, the two bridge syncs that are not plain sets, the\ncompletion rule with its numbers against all eleven seeded profiles, and the\nDATEDIFF(MONTH) bug that was making every closed job one month short.\n\n2.55 records the push: the seven remote URLs, the credentials that came out of\nHOW_TO_RUN first, and the two more that were hiding outside the credentials\ntable — G20 quoted a password and a verify script had one hardcoded.\n\nG0 is closed, and so are its three stale references elsewhere in the file: two\n\"everything is on one machine\" warnings and one demo-checklist item. A closed\ngap that is still warned about in three other places is a gap nobody trusts the\nstatus of.\n\nNext Action is 3E — the API and then the screens — with the two things the API\nhas to hold: UserUid and ViewerSchoolId from the token only, and one route to a\nresume.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c224c72984d4377129db3c560987afd52be89e71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/trees/c224c72984d4377129db3c560987afd52be89e71"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/commits/2cc3856914a38f103f16a612c923c4717e51e809","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/2cc3856914a38f103f16a612c923c4717e51e809","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zoeNoAKDJjYzM4NTY5MTRhMzhmMTAzZjE2YTYxMmM5MjNjNDcxN2U1MWU4MDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/5704749012ed6a7e67892e10d803fe53b7470361","sha":"5704749012ed6a7e67892e10d803fe53b7470361","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/5704749012ed6a7e67892e10d803fe53b7470361"}],"sha":"2cc3856914a38f103f16a612c923c4717e51e809","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/2cc3856914a38f103f16a612c923c4717e51e809"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/5704749012ed6a7e67892e10d803fe53b7470361/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T23:35:52Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T23:35:52Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"Move local credentials out of the repository\n\nHOW_TO_RUN.md carried plaintext passwords for the five seeded accounts,\nincluding a generated superadmin password. The file''s own warning said to strip\nthem before sharing outside the team — pushing to GitHub is that moment, and a\npassword in a repository''s history outlives the decision to remove it.\n\nThey now live in local-accounts.md, which is gitignored. The table keeps the\nemails and what each account demonstrates, so the doc still explains the system;\nonly the secrets left.\n\nTwo more were hiding outside the credentials table: PROJECT_MEMORY''s G20 quoted\nthe seeded teacher password, and scripts/verify/signin-check.mjs had one\nhardcoded. The script now reads JP_SCHOOL_PASSWORD from the environment and\nfails with a pointer to local-accounts.md rather than silently signing in as\nnobody.\n\nlocal-accounts.md also records how to rebuild the accounts from nothing — the\nreal registration endpoints for schools and teachers, and JP.Tools.SeedAdmin\n--generate for the administrator — because on a new machine the file will not\nbe there, and the right answer then is to rebuild rather than to ask somebody\nfor passwords over chat.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"af1ba755df494d17e03114faced3bed8ca6847bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/trees/af1ba755df494d17e03114faced3bed8ca6847bd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/commits/5704749012ed6a7e67892e10d803fe53b7470361","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/5704749012ed6a7e67892e10d803fe53b7470361","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zoeNoAKDU3MDQ3NDkwMTJlZDZhN2U2Nzg5MmUxMGQ4MDNmZTUzYjc0NzAzNjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/5ed0a302c127499a079bdaa051d3adce6fcc159e","sha":"5ed0a302c127499a079bdaa051d3adce6fcc159e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/5ed0a302c127499a079bdaa051d3adce6fcc159e"}],"sha":"5704749012ed6a7e67892e10d803fe53b7470361","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/5704749012ed6a7e67892e10d803fe53b7470361"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/5ed0a302c127499a079bdaa051d3adce6fcc159e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T23:26:27Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T23:26:27Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"PROJECT_MEMORY: Phase 3C — decision 2.53, G19 and G21 closed, G22 opened\n\n2.53 records the scope resolver and why it is an inline TVF, the bridge-sync\npattern in the form 3D should copy, why the public profile is a separate\nprocedure rather than a flag, the three refusals on branch delete including the\none written now for Phase 4, and the two production bugs that running a real\nregistration exposed.\n\nG19 and G21 both closed. G22 opened in their place: the scope resolver is a\nconvention with a test behind it, not enforcement — nothing stops a future list\nprocedure hand-rolling its own version, and that copy is where an IDOR would\nlive. Phases 4 and 5 both stand on it.\n\nHOW_TO_RUN: the St Mary''s row now describes an account that works.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8b8c797c429719da510fc37c793704a5462f3b74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/trees/8b8c797c429719da510fc37c793704a5462f3b74"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/commits/5ed0a302c127499a079bdaa051d3adce6fcc159e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/5ed0a302c127499a079bdaa051d3adce6fcc159e","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zoeNoAKDVlZDBhMzAyYzEyNzQ5OWEwNzliZGFhMDUxZDNhZGNlNmZjYzE1OWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/1e3df3878c1725152e729d995d81b68ad8856fc7","sha":"1e3df3878c1725152e729d995d81b68ad8856fc7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/1e3df3878c1725152e729d995d81b68ad8856fc7"}],"sha":"5ed0a302c127499a079bdaa051d3adce6fcc159e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/5ed0a302c127499a079bdaa051d3adce6fcc159e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/1e3df3878c1725152e729d995d81b68ad8856fc7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T12:42:57Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T12:42:57Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"PROJECT_MEMORY: Phase 3B — decision 2.52, G12 closed, G19-G21 opened\n\nG12 is closed: the table exists, eleven profiles are backfilled, and eleven\nTEACHER_FREE subscriptions are assigned. Both halves are evidenced by the\nverification query rather than asserted.\n\nThree new gaps, and two of them exist so that \"G12 closed\" cannot be misread:\n\n  G19 — an Active school account with no school row at all, seeded in Phase 1\n        before the approval engine. It has a plan now and will never have a\n        school, because provisioning runs from an approval request and there is\n        none behind it.\n  G20 — every teacher field is invented. Anything in Phase 4 or 5 that appears\n        to work against this data is working against data we made up. The full\n        list of seeded accounts and exactly which fields were invented is\n        recorded now, while it is known; reconstructing it later would be\n        guesswork against a live database.\n  G21 — signup still does not create a profile. The backfill fixed the accounts\n        that existed; a teacher registering tomorrow falls into the same gap\n        that was just closed, one account at a time. Its test is the\n        verification query: check A is 0 today and becomes 1 after one signup.\n\nNext Action is 3C, whose first task is G21 rather than a feature.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d6b63e6ad369e22c07350d567d5e5553d9a575c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/trees/d6b63e6ad369e22c07350d567d5e5553d9a575c2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/git/commits/1e3df3878c1725152e729d995d81b68ad8856fc7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/1e3df3878c1725152e729d995d81b68ad8856fc7","node_id":"C_kwDOT4zoeNoAKDFlM2RmMzg3OGMxNzI1MTUyZTcyOWQ5OTVkODFiNjhhZDg4NTZmYzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commit/0043bbfb66e6460c6a8e268c99724120e2ca4848","sha":"0043bbfb66e6460c6a8e268c99724120e2ca4848","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/0043bbfb66e6460c6a8e268c99724120e2ca4848"}],"sha":"1e3df3878c1725152e729d995d81b68ad8856fc7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/1e3df3878c1725152e729d995d81b68ad8856fc7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105528886?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tarun1515","id":105528886,"login":"Tarun1515","node_id":"U_kgDOBko-Ng","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tarun1515","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Tarun1515/jp-docs/commits/0043bbfb66e6460c6a8e268c99724120e2ca4848/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T11:03:06Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T11:03:06Z","email":"bhardwajtarun22@gmail.com","name":"Tarun Bhardwaj"},"message":"PROJECT_MEMORY: Phase 3A — decision 2.51, Next Action 3B\n\n2.51 records the two ALTERs against the spec, the full list of columns\nclassified as `date` and the test that proves it, every business key added with\nits reason, and the three places I disagreed with the brief — a FilePath key on\nschool photos, and deliberately no unique index on teacher documents or\nexperiences, with the reasoning for each.\n\nG12 updated: 3A did the first of its three things. t_app_teachers exists and is\nempty, which is a different problem from it being absent — the gap stays open\nuntil 3B backfills and assigns TEACHER_FREE.\n\nNext Action is 3B, with what 3A already did to make it re-runnable: the filtered\nunique index on UserUid refuses a duplicate profile rather than silently\nskipping it, so the backfill has to treat that as \"already done\" the way\nprovisioning does (2.48).\n\nThe Milestone 1 pre-demo checklist moves to \"Uske baad\" rather than being\ndropped — it is still outstanding.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"295